&lt;p&gt;Lyft is looking for a bright, pragmatic, and self-motivated employment attorney with 4+ years of employment counseling and litigation experience to join our growing global Legal team. The ideal candidate will leverage their prior law firm and/or in-house experience to provide thoughtful, timely, practical and business-minded legal advice primarily to the professionals on Lyft’s Employee Relations and People teams across the globe. You must have experience litigating and/or counseling on compliance with federal and state anti-discrimination/harassment/retaliation laws, preferably including analysis of issues under California law. Prior in-house or seconded technology company experience is preferred but not required. The successful candidate will be an entrepreneurial and resourceful self-starter, comfortable working in a fast-paced and dynamic environment, excellent at building strong relationships and interested in learning more about supporting a global workforce.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide pragmatic day-to-day employment advice and counseling on a broad range of employment issues in order to balance business impact and legal risk including HR practices, performance management, terminations, leaves of absence, investigations, and employee accommodations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate pre-litigation and litigation matters.&amp;nbsp; Develop and implement strategies for early resolution (as appropriate) and work with outside counsel as appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide guidance and Interpret policies and procedures, incorporating knowledge of state and federal employment laws (e.g., FMLA, ADA, FLSA, NLRA, and Title VII and equivalent state and international laws).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide legal counsel and support to a global workforce.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Lyft’s Employee Relations and People team professionals on employee complaints and investigations, performance management, and accommodations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with other members of the Employment Legal Team and People Team to develop strong processes to ensure compliance with applicable state, federal and local laws.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and deliver training to managers and employees -- candidates must be comfortable with public speaking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor important developments in employment law in jurisdictions across the country and internationally, striving to spot trends in their infancy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work and build trust with cross-functional partners from teams across the Legal Department and the Company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel from time-to-time as necessary to service internal clients; develop cross-office relationships; and attend legal proceedings/negotiations.\&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years practicing employment law at a leading law firm and/or in-house, with experience and/or interest in advice and counseling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior in-house experience and expertise supporting a global workforce is a plus but not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active and in good standing with a State Bar and eligible to practice in the relevant jurisdiction where you are located.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;J.D. from a top-tier law school&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent problem-solving capabilities, judgment, communication (written and verbal) and interpersonal skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adept at thinking creatively (and strategically!) on your feet, conveying grace under pressure, and simultaneously managing complex workloads, multiple client demands, and shifting priorities all while instilling confidence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resourceful self-starter and have a passion for results. Embody Lyft’s culture, and operate with high standards and ethics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Great medical, dental, and vision insurance options with additional programs available when enrolled&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family building benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Child care and pet benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) plan with company match to help save for your future&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In addition to 12 observed holidays, salaried team members have discretionary paid time off, hourly team members have 15 days paid time off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;18 weeks of paid parental leave. Biological, adoptive, and foster parents are all eligible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subsidized commuter benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly Lyft credits and complimentary Lyft Pink membership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
