&lt;p&gt;Flexdrive is a subsidiary of Lyft that works together with Lyft teams to realize our shared mission.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Flexdrive builds the operational backbone for the future of mobility. As a fleet management leader and Lyft subsidiary, the company extends its expertise into autonomous vehicle infrastructure — managing the physical operations that keep fleets safe, available, and performing at scale. The Nashville depot is the first proof point in a multi-market expansion.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Operations Manager, AV Depot, the Associate Operations Manager is the second leadership layer at the Nashville AV depot. This role exists because one Operations Manager cannot provide the people leadership, floor coverage, and operational bandwidth a 24/7 depot of this scale requires.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Associate Operations Manager carries ownership across two critical business workstreams: workforce scheduling support and process standards compliance. Fleet Operations Leads report to the Operations Manager — but during mid shifts, the Associate Operations Manager is the operational authority on the floor, directing their work, setting the quality standard, and serving as their most experienced resource and mentor.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a management role with a floor orientation. The Associate Operations Manager is present, coaching, directing, and executing alongside the team — while simultaneously carrying business responsibilities that directly impact depot readiness and partner compliance. This role is the bridge between the Fleet Operations Lead layer and the Operations Manager.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scheduling &amp;amp; Workforce Planning Support&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owns the depot schedule — building, maintaining, and adjusting shift coverage across all teams to ensure the depot is consistently staffed and operationally ready.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitors attendance, manages real-time coverage gaps, and proactively addresses workforce trends before they become operational problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partners with the Operations Manager on workforce planning, surfacing scheduling risks and recommendations with enough lead time to act.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Training Program Execution &amp;amp; Certification Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owns the planning and coordination of training program execution across all shift teams — ensuring Fleet Operations Associates and Fleet Operations Leads are scheduled, prepared, and on track to complete required partner certifications, safety refreshers, and qualification renewals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintains certification and qualification records for the team, flagging upcoming renewals and escalating compliance risks to the Operations Manager before they become audit findings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partners with the Program Lead Trainer to ensure qualified trainers are in place, training resources are available, and delivery stays consistent across shift teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Floor Execution &amp;amp; Quality Standards&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the day-to-day execution of critical operational systems and processes for our 24/7 AV fleet management operations, including depot layout adherence, vehicle flow (charging, cleaning, maintenance, staging, diagnostics), parts management, and data handling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serves as the operational authority during mid shifts — directing Fleet Operations Leads and Fleet Operations Associates on task execution, resolving workflow conflicts, and holding the floor accountable to depot performance targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owns quality on shift: vehicle readiness, safety inspections, and quality standards — inspecting, enforcing, and setting the standard by working alongside the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintains accurate shift documentation and manages shift handoffs with discipline, ensuring the incoming Fleet Operations Lead has full situational awareness and no items fall through the gap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fleet Operations Lead Mentorship &amp;amp; Operational Direction&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Directs Fleet Operations Leads operationally on shift — task priorities, execution decisions, real-time escalations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serves as the most experienced senior leader in the building in absence of the Operations Manager, providing in-the-moment coaching and surfacing structured performance observations to the Operations Manager.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of progressive experience in operational leadership, with a strong understanding of autonomous vehicle (AV) or complex fleet operational environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of launching and scaling new operational sites or programs, including accountability for facilities,&amp;nbsp; team performance, and operational outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated expertise in safety management and regulatory compliance within transportation, automotive, or similar regulated industries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience executing incident response and coordinating multi-vendor support in complex operational environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work a flexible schedule, including nights, weekends, and holidays as needed, to effectively support and lead a 24/7 AV depot operation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional leadership in training execution and team development, with the ability to lead high-performing teams in safety-critical operations at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and data-driven mindset, with the ability to translate operational data into actionable decisions and surface clear recommendations to leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated leadership ability in fast-paced, high-accountability environments, with excellent communication and interpersonal skills to drive cross-functional alignment and lead on-site operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Engineering, Business, Operations Management, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Great medical, dental, and vision insurance options with additional programs available when enrolled&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family building benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Child care and pet benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) plan with company match to help save for your future&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In addition to 12 observed holidays, salaried team members have discretionary paid time off, hourly team members have 15 days paid time off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;18 weeks of paid parental leave. Biological, adoptive, and foster parents are all eligible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subsidized commuter benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly Lyft credits and complimentary Lyft Pink membership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;: For this role, candidates must reside in states registered for Flexdrive Services LLC.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is on-site at a Lyft Flexdrive hub or office location full time. &lt;strong&gt;#Onsite&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The expected base pay range for this position in the Nashville area is $88,560 - $110,700, not inclusive of potential equity offering, bonus or benefits. Salary ranges are dependent on a variety of factors, including qualifications, experience and geographic location. Your recruiter can share more information about the salary range specific to your working location and other factors during the hiring process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Flexdrive is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to an inclusive workplace that fosters belonging. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regards to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, age, genetic information, or any other basis prohibited by law. Flexdrive also strives for a healthy and safe workplace and strictly prohibits harassment of any kind. Flexdrive will also consider employment for qualified applicants with criminal histories consistent with applicable federal, state and local law.&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":4135513002,"name":"AV & Fleet Operations","child_ids":[],"parent_id":4135512002}],"offices":[{"id":4118460002,"name":"Nashville AV Depot","location":"Nashville, Tennessee, Nashville","child_ids":[],"parent_id":4038194002}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":null,"ai_opt_out_request_url":null},{"absolute_url":"https://app.careerpuck.com/job-board/lyft/job/8839156002?gh_jid=8839156002","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"education":"education_optional","employment":"employment_required","internal_job_id":6538486002,"location":{"name":"San Francisco, CA"},"metadata":[{"id":4345907002,"name":"Career Site Category","value":"Growth","value_type":"single_select"}],"id":8839156002,"updated_at":"2026-10-19T18:43:36-04:00","requisition_id":"111211","title":"AV Program Manager","company_name":"Lyft","first_published":"2026-09-25T12:02:18-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;At Lyft, our purpose is to serve and connect. We aim to achieve this by cultivating a work environment where all team members belong and have the opportunity to thrive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Flexdrive, Lyft&#39;s wholly-owned fleet management subsidiary, is undergoing a transformational shift from traditional rideshare fleet operations to autonomous vehicle fleet ownership and operations. We are seeking an AV Program Manager to help drive the cross-functional operating plan that will prepare Flexdrive to receive, staff, and operate AV fleets at scale domestically and abroad.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role supports the operational backbone of Flexdrive&#39;s AV readiness initiative. You will maintain the program timeline, coordinate cross-functional workstreams spanning infrastructure, people, fleet operations, treasury, legal, and finance, and help ensure that requirements are tracked, dependencies are surfaced, and deployment milestones are met. You will work closely with workstream leads across Operations, Strategy, Infrastructure, Finance,&amp;nbsp; Legal, Analytics, and People.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you thrive in ambiguity, can bring structure to complex multi-workstream programs, and have a bias toward action, this role is for you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1. Program Planning &amp;amp; Execution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain the program timeline for Flexdrive AV Operating Readiness, tracking deliverables and dependencies across workstreams: Strategic Planning, Infrastructure, Analytics, People, Fleet Operations, Treasury, Finance, and Legal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain the program&#39;s RAID log (Risks, Assumptions, Issues, Dependencies), surfacing cross-functional blockers with clear context for escalation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support weekly leadership syncs and monthly deep-dive reviews, including preparation, presentation and follow-through.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate upstream decisions (partner agreements, market selections, ) into operational requirements, updating the readiness roadmap accordingly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2. Cross-Functional Coordination&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a connection point between workstream leads, helping ensure infrastructure timelines align with hiring plans, capital deployment schedules match construction milestones, and fleet operations readiness tracks to vehicle delivery dates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the central hub across cross-functional internal teams supporting the program; drive alignment on priorities and decisions, escalate issues with the right context, and be accountable for resolution&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with People and Operations to help sequence hiring, training, and certification programs ahead of vehicle arrivals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with FP&amp;amp;A and Treasury to track investment spend against the capital deployment schedule and flag variance early.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3. Stakeholder Communication &amp;amp; Reporting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and deliver clear status reporting to program leadership and workstream stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure cross-functional stakeholders stay aligned on expectations, deliverables, and timelines throughout the program.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain market readiness scorecards that provide visibility into each market&#39;s progress against deployment milestones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain program documentation including decision logs, meeting notes, and workstream status trackers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4. Process Support &amp;amp; Operational Excellence&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help design and implement the program management operating model for AV readiness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and build process improvements across workstreams, using data to help optimize timelines and resource allocation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build repeatable playbooks for market readiness that scale&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5 years of experience in program management, business operations, or a similar cross-functional role, ideally within high-growth tech, fleet management, logistics, or infrastructure-heavy environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills with the ability to translate operational detail into clear updates for cross-functional stakeholders&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational skills, with experience tracking timelines, risks, and dependencies across multiple workstreams, and adapting whatever program management tools or frameworks the situation calls for&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to navigate ambiguity and operate effectively in a fast-moving environment where priorities and processes continue to evolve&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong relationship-building skills, with the ability to organize effective working groups and resolve conflicts around program processes and goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical mindset with ability to identify risks, quantify trade-offs, and recommend courses of action with imperfect information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience preparing materials for and presenting to senior leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with infrastructure buildout programs (depot construction, facility standup, real estate development).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in capital intensive projects, fleet management, automotive, mobility, or autonomous vehicle operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing programs that span domestic and international markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a subsidiary or business unit operating within a larger corporate parent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Great medical, dental, and vision insurance options with additional programs available when enrolled&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family building benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Child care and pet benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) plan with company match to help save for your future&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In addition to 12 observed holidays, salaried team members have discretionary paid time off, hourly team members have 15 days paid time off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;18 weeks of paid parental leave. Biological, adoptive, and foster parents are all eligible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subsidized commuter benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly Lyft credits and complimentary Lyft Pink membership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lyft is an equal opportunity employer committed to an inclusive workplace that fosters belonging. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regards to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, age, genetic information, or any other basis prohibited by law. We also consider qualified applicants with criminal histories consistent with applicable federal, state and local law.&lt;/p&gt;
