&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for generating and customizing reports summarizing business and financial data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and update business intelligence tools, databases, dashboards, systems and other methods to capture, analyze, and estimate customer business requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, maintain, and enhance Anaplan models based on design specifications and best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate business requirements into functional model components and develop and maintain data integrations between Anaplan and source systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design various financial planning and analysis (FP&amp;amp;A) use cases, including budgeting, forecasting, and financial reporting, as well as develop and implement automation routines and data integrations to streamline FP&amp;amp;A processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create business intelligence tools and systems, including user-friendly dashboards and reports for business users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform data validation and reconciliation to ensure data accuracy and provide end-user support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Position requires Bachelor&#39;s degree or foreign equivalent in Computer Science, Engineering, or related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3 years of experience in job offered, Engineering, or related occupation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 3 years’ experience with business intelligence and process flows to design custom solutions with Oracle ERP Cloud or Oracle Fusion Cloud applications, including finance, SCM, BICC, and OTBI reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 3 years’ experience with Anaplan or similar enterprise performance management for modeling, building, planning, analysis, and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing plans and project management techniques to translate unstructured business problems into defined requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience transforming data and automating processes using Python or a similar scripting language.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Great medical, dental, and vision insurance options with additional programs available when enrolled&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family building benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Child care and pet benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) plan to help save for your future&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In addition to 12 observed holidays, salaried team members have discretionary paid time off, hourly team members have 15 days paid time off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;18 weeks of paid parental leave. Biological, adoptive, and foster parents are all eligible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subsidized commuter benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lyft Pink - Lyft team members get an exclusive opportunity to test new benefits of our Ridership Program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
