&lt;li&gt;Develop and fit statistical, machine learning, or optimization models. Deploy production-grade models that solve business problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, implement, and analyse different types of experiments, and facilitate data-driven and informed decision making and prioritization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish metrics and development measurement methodologies to monitor the health of our products, as well as the impacts on user and marketplace outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform deep dive analysis to gain a deeper understanding of the problem and uncover new product and business opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive collaboration and coordination with cross-functional teams. Communicate findings to a broad audience consisting of Product, Engineering, and executive leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;M.S. or Ph.D. in Machine Learning, Operations Research, Statistics, Computer Science or other quantitative fields&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1-4+ years professional experience for PhDs or 3-5+ years for Master’s in a Data Science role in a technology company setting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience with building and evaluating optimization or machine learning models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with Python and working in a production coding environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for solving unstructured and non-standard mathematical problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;End-to-end experience with data, including querying, aggregation, analysis, and visualization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong verbal and written communication skills, and ability to collaborate and communicate with others to solve a problem&lt;/li&gt;
