like FreeNow, Gett, and TBR, the technology, P&amp;amp;Ls, and org charts have continued to run as separate regional stacks. Global B2B exists to change that: to build a common platform that compounds instead of resetting with every new deal, powering existing US demand while unlocking the lines of business we&#39;ve had to turn away.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Technical Program Manager who can bring order, rigor, and momentum to a program of this scale: one that spans multiple P&amp;amp;Ls, multiple geographies, and multiple functions, all moving toward one plan. You&#39;ll report directly to Rishi Dean (VP of Technology and DRI of Global B2B) and will be the connective tissue that turns strategy into a sequenced, tracked, and delivered program. You&#39;re technically strong, comfortable operating in ambiguity, and skilled at getting people who don&#39;t report to you to move together toward a shared date.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end program management of Global B2B: build and maintain the integrated cross-org plan, name every dependency with an owner and a date, and keep the plan honest as priorities shift across Rider, Lyft Europe, Lyft Business, Global Growth, and Finance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run the standing sequencing forum where teams bring business cases, resolve competing priorities, and arbitrate capacity across client commitments, foundational platform work, and expansion opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive execution across the platform&#39;s core layers (e.g., application, sales systems, financial/billing, partner integration, and marketing stack), coordinating single-threaded owners and surfacing where design authority and funding models still need to be settled&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and report program health across every revenue line (US B2B, EU B2B, EU B2G, Chauffeur, Partner/Protocol) and escalate risks to PDT early, before they become date slips&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the joint planning work between Global B2B and Lyft Europe to align the FreeNow and Gett integration with the Europe roaming and app-launch timeline, converting shared assumptions into written, dated commitments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the annual planning cycle for Global B2B, translating scope and business cases into resourced, sequenced initiatives from September through November&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and enforce a consistent product standard across the portfolio, including a scoping gate that keeps requirement changes from silently consuming central capacity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and run the onboarding path for newly acquired or newly connected businesses (following FreeNow, Gett, and TBR) covering platform, systems, P&amp;amp;L, reporting, and GTM motion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Partnerships, Rider, and MBA to bring AI/agentic surfaces and protocol work into the Global B2B plan from the start, rather than reconciling separate efforts after the fact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate program status, risks, and decisions clearly to stakeholders ranging from individual engineers to executive leadership, in a style that is direct, fact-forward, and free of jargon&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EXPERIENCE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in Technical Program Management, Program/Project Management, or a related role, ideally spanning platform, product, and go-to-market work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to build and hold one integrated plan across multiple orgs with different priorities, scale, and cadences, with a thorough understanding of dependency management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience standing up or running a sequencing/prioritization forum where competing business cases are arbitrated against shared capacity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable operating autonomously in situations of extreme ambiguity, with only high-level direction, and translating that ambiguity into a written, dated plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to communicate highly technical and cross-functional problems and solutions at every level, from individual contributor to C-level executive&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with platform or infrastructure programs that serve multiple business lines or P&amp;amp;Ls, including shared systems like CRM, billing/invoicing, or partner integration layers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background supporting or working alongside M&amp;amp;A integration (systems, org, or GTM integration) is a strong plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent organizational and planning skills, with the attention to detail to keep a multi-quarter, multi-org program on track&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to influence, negotiate, and inspire others in a matrixed environment where you don&#39;t have direct authority over most of the people you depend on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Great medical, dental, and vision insurance options with additional programs available when enrolled&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family building benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Child care and pet benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) plan to help save for your future&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In addition to 12 observed holidays, salaried team members have discretionary paid time off, hourly team members have 15 days paid time off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;18 weeks of paid parental leave. Biological, adoptive, and foster parents are all eligible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subsidized commuter benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lyft Pink - Lyft team members get an exclusive opportunity to test new benefits of our Ridership Program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Lyft is an equal opportunity employer committed to an inclusive workplace that fosters belonging. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regards to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, age, genetic information, or any other basis prohibited by law. We also consider qualified applicants with criminal histories consistent with applicable federal, state and local law.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This role is fully remote in the US, candidates for this role must be based in the United States &lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;#Remote&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The expected base pay range for this position is [$217,120] - [$271,400]. In addition to the base pay, this role is eligible for competitive equity awards, bonuses, and benefits. You can read more about Lyft’s employee benefits &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.lyft.com/careers/life-at-lyft&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Total compensation is dependent on a variety of factors, including qualifications, experience, and geographic location. Your recruiter can share more information about the salary range specific to your working location and other factors during the hiring process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":4135522002,"name":"Media & Lyft Business","child_ids":[4135523002,4092657002,4069022002],"parent_id":4042810002}],"offices":[{"id":4048722002,"name":"Flex - US","location":"United States, , United States","child_ids":[],"parent_id":4031978002}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":null,"ai_opt_out_request_url":null},{"absolute_url":"https://app.careerpuck.com/job-board/lyft/job/8861939002?gh_jid=8861939002","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"education":"education_optional","employment":"employment_required","internal_job_id":6547774002,"location":{"name":"New York, NY; San Francisco, CA"},"metadata":[{"id":4345907002,"name":"Career Site Category","value":"Communications","value_type":"single_select"}],"id":8861939002,"updated_at":"2026-10-19T18:43:36-04:00","requisition_id":"111235","title":"Director, Product & Brand Communications","company_name":"Lyft","first_published":"2026-10-01T19:45:38-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;At Lyft, our purpose is to serve and connect. To do this, we start with our own community by fostering a respectful and diverse organization where every voice is heard, valued, and empowered to contribute to our shared success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a strategic and visionary Director of Product and Brand Communications to play a pivotal leadership role in building a fresh take on an iconic brand. This highly visible and cross-functional position will drive the company’s product narrative, giving riders and drivers compelling reasons to choose Lyft.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a vocal cross-functional partner with significant influence, you&#39;ll collaborate across departments to shape our brand story and product narratives. This role demands a strategic thinker who can craft compelling narratives for multiple audiences including riders, drivers, regulators, and the broader business community.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The successful candidate will be a resourceful self-starter who thrives in dynamic, fast-paced environments, demonstrating agility and adaptability as our company and industry evolve. You&#39;ll own the process for building and launching brand and product moments through multi-channel, earned media programs including narrative development, product demos, event planning, editorial extensions, and influencer engagement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an opportunity to join a fun and hungry team and have a profound impact on the company. The role reports to the Vice President of Communications.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define compelling consumer and technology narratives that support the company’s broader narrative and vision, and build a strategic and creative communications plan that strengthens Lyft’s image and reputation with consumers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide strategic leadership for the Product and Brand Communications team, setting the vision, developing long-term plans, and fostering a high-performing team through mentorship, coaching, and professional development opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead our content strategy, including AEO efforts&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the organization&#39;s communication strategy through cohesive messaging and orchestrated narrative drum beats, demonstrating the ability to influence and collaborate with senior leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a vocal leader and strategic partner across functions to ensure alignment and buy-in on narratives and strategic plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with product, marketing, legal, and policy teams to ensure consistent messaging and a unified brand experience across all touchpoints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain media relationships with top-tier outlets, driving public relations campaigns that promote brand awareness and manage the company&#39;s public image.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build integrated communications capability including across new and emerging platforms. Develop and maintain regular reporting mechanisms to communicate progress, insights, and recommendations to leadership and key stakeholders.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze data and insights to optimize communication strategies and maximize impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of communications experience with demonstrated success in technology products and services, especially in two-sided and/or highly regulated marketplaces. Public company experience preferred.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading high performing teams and fostering collaborative cultures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience building constructive relationships with top tier reporters, editors and influencers. Has great media relationships / experiences and isn’t afraid to pick up the phone to create new ones.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience as a trusted communications advisor to business partners and executives, with demonstrated ability to influence at the senior leadership level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Not afraid to take big swings and go for the win!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience shaping and developing narratives that align with the company mission and resonate with audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrives in complex situations and fast-paced environments. Dives deep and asks questions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communications skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-starter, independently motivated, leads oneself and influences others. Has experience managing a team in dynamic industries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Great medical, dental, and vision insurance options with additional programs available when enrolled&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family building benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Child care and pet benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) plan to help save for your future&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In addition to 12 observed holidays, salaried team members have discretionary paid time off, hourly team members have 15 days paid time off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;18 weeks of paid parental leave. Biological, adoptive, and foster parents are all eligible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subsidized commuter benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lyft Pink - Lyft team members get an exclusive opportunity to test new benefits of our Ridership Program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Lyft is an equal opportunity employer committed to an inclusive workplace that fosters belonging. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regards to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, age, genetic information, or any other basis prohibited by law. We also consider qualified applicants with criminal histories consistent with applicable federal, state and local law.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Lyft highly values having employees working in-office to foster a collaborative work environment and company culture. This role will be in-office on a hybrid schedule — Team Members will be expected to work in the office 3 days per week on Mondays, Wednesdays, and Thursdays. Lyft considers working in the office at least 3 days per week to be an essential function of this hybrid role. Your recruiter can share more information about the various in-office perks Lyft offers. Additionally, hybrid roles have the flexibility to work from anywhere for up to 4 weeks per year. #Hybrid&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The expected base pay range for this position in San Francisco is $200-240K. In addition to the base pay, this role is eligible for competitive equity awards, bonuses, and benefits. You can read more about Lyft’s employee benefits &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.lyft.com/careers/life-at-lyft&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Total compensation is dependent on a variety of factors, including qualifications, experience, and geographic location. Your recruiter can share more information about the salary range specific to your working location and other factors during the hiring process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":4038190002,"name":"Executive","child_ids":[4047184002,4048791002,4053407002,4047188002,4112306002,4047190002,4053405002,4055377002,4047189002,4047185002,4065652002,4081661002,4047187002,4047191002,4053408002,4056422002,4051163002,4053406002,4047186002],"parent_id":null}],"offices":[{"id":4000997002,"name":"New York Office","location":"New York, New York, United States","child_ids":[],"parent_id":4032338002},{"id":4000998002,"name":"San Francisco Office","location":"San Francisco, California, United States","child_ids":[],"parent_id":4031979002}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":null,"ai_opt_out_request_url":null},{"absolute_url":"https://app.careerpuck.com/job-board/lyft/job/8782314002?gh_jid=8782314002","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"education":"education_optional","employment":"employment_required","internal_job_id":6513399002,"location":{"name":"New York, NY; San Francisco, CA"},"metadata":[{"id":4345907002,"name":"Career Site Category","value":"Operations","value_type":"single_select"}],"id":8782314002,"updated_at":"2026-10-19T18:43:36-04:00","requisition_id":"111150","title":"Director, Trust & Safety","company_name":"Lyft","first_published":"2026-09-15T13:28:26-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;At Lyft, our purpose is to serve and connect. We aim to achieve this by cultivating a work environment where all team members belong and have the opportunity to thrive. Safety is fundamental to the Lyft experience and to the trust riders, drivers, and our broader communities place in our platform. Lyft’s Safety and Customer Care team works through product, technology, data, policy, and operations to prevent harm before it happens, respond compassionately when it does, and continuously learn from every incident in efforts to make Lyft the safest way to get around.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an experienced safety leader with deep &lt;strong&gt;Trust &amp;amp; Safety &lt;/strong&gt;experience&amp;nbsp; to help turn Lyft’s Trust &amp;amp; Safety strategy into impact at scale, with the final shape of this role informed by the strengths of the leader we bring on. This is a highly visible leadership role within Lyft’s Safety &amp;amp; Customer Care organization. You will report to the Senior Director and General Manager of Trust &amp;amp; Safety and sit on the Trust &amp;amp; Safety leadership team. You will additionally partner deeply with Product, Engineering, Data Science, Research &amp;amp; Design, Legal, Compliance, Risk, Communications, Finance, and other teams across Lyft.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate is an exceptional operator and people leader with Trust &amp;amp; Safety expertise, strong strategic judgment, and a track record of leading complex, high-stakes Trust &amp;amp; Safety organizations at scale. You can move fluidly between setting strategy with senior executives, developing leaders, overseeing large global operations and budgets, and diving into an emerging safety issue when the situation demands it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead Global Safety Compliance &amp;amp; Risk&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee Lyft’s global safety compliance, transparency, and risk functions, supporting strong functional leaders and individual contributors on your team and strengthening capabilities as Lyft scales globally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set direction across compliance readiness, safety transparency reporting, and risk assessment, ensuring strong governance and execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Legal, Regulatory Compliance, and business leaders to anticipate emerging requirements and risks across markets, products, and business models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure material risks, dependencies, and gaps are surfaced early, with clear ownership and senior-level visibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead Trust &amp;amp; Safety Business Enablement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide the functions that turn Trust &amp;amp; Safety strategy and policy into scalable execution across the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure teams are aligned around clear priorities, ownership, and outcomes while empowering functional leaders to drive execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strengthen the playbooks, operating mechanisms, and cross-functional connections needed to safely launch new products, features, markets, and experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help evolve Lyft’s Trust &amp;amp; Safety operating model as the business grows in scale and complexity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead Trust &amp;amp; Safety Partnerships&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the Trust &amp;amp; Safety strategy for strategic partners, acquisitions, and businesses joining Lyft’s expanding global ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support partnership leaders in building scalable approaches across different products, markets, operating models, regulatory environments, and risk profiles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure partners are effectively integrated into Lyft’s safety ecosystem, with clear standards, ownership, governance, and escalation paths.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Surface partnership risks and readiness early, enabling Lyft to grow and integrate new businesses safely.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive the Operating Rhythm&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help translate strategy into priorities, operating plans, resource decisions, and measurable outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the organization’s planning, prioritization, goal-setting, and business review rhythms, ensuring clear decisions, accountability, and follow-through.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the General Manager of Trust &amp;amp; Safety with Lyft-wide and executive efforts, including strategic planning, Board and executive preparation, and cross-functional initiatives requiring senior-level coordination.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Distill complex issues into clear, decision-ready narratives and recommendations for executives and cross-functional leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build and Lead Exceptional Teams&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead talented individual contributors and people managers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build an organization with clear accountability, strong decision-making, high standards, and the ability to operate effectively through ambiguity and change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop leaders who independently own large, complex areas while maintaining strong alignment across the broader Trust &amp;amp; Safety organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create an environment where teams combine urgency with sound judgment, challenge assumptions constructively, learn from mistakes, and are grounded in the experiences of riders and drivers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of relevant professional experience, with significant experience in Trust &amp;amp; Safety, safety, risk, integrity, customer operations, platform operations, or another closely related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep, direct experience leading at least two Trust &amp;amp; Safety functions (e.g. product and policy; policy and operations; operations and programs) at scale is required.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading Trust &amp;amp; Safety at a scaled consumer technology, marketplace, mobility, social, sharing-economy, or other platform business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of significant people leadership experience, including demonstrated success managing individual contributors, managers or senior leaders, and leaders of leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience owning significant budgets and making strategic tradeoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building scalable operating models, processes, governance mechanisms, and performance-management systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and financial judgment, with the ability to use data to diagnose problems, evaluate tradeoffs, develop business cases, and allocate resources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional executive communication and stakeholder-management skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience integrating Trust &amp;amp; Safety operations following acquisitions, strategic partnerships, international expansion, or entry into new business lines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operationalizing regulatory or compliance requirements across complex products and global operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with safety transparency reporting, regulatory reporting, audits, or other complex external accountability programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using AI, automation, and advanced analytics to improve operational quality, efficiency, detection, decision-making, or customer experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Considerations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Trust &amp;amp; Safety work can involve sensitive subject matter. In this role, you may be exposed to descriptions, reports, or other content involving violence, sexual assault, harassment, or other potentially graphic or distressing safety incidents. You may also be asked to participate in legal proceedings (e.g. depositions), related to Lyft’s Trust &amp;amp; Safety practices or specific matters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Great medical, dental, and vision insurance options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family building benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In addition to 12 observed holidays, salaried team members have unlimited paid time off, hourly team members have 15 days paid time off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) plan to help save for your future&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;18 weeks of paid parental leave. Biological, adoptive, and foster parents are all eligible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pre-tax commuter benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lyft Pink - Lyft team members get an exclusive opportunity to test new benefits of our Ridership Program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Lyft is an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer committed to an inclusive and diverse workplace. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regards to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status or any other basis prohibited by law. We also consider qualified applicants with criminal histories consistent with applicable federal, state and local law.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This role will be in-office on a hybrid schedule — Team Members are expected to work in the office 3 days per week on Mondays, Wednesdays, and Thursdays. Additionally, hybrid roles have the flexibility to work from anywhere for up to 4 weeks per year.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The expected range of pay for this position in the San Francisco or New York areas is $203,000 - $253,750. Salary ranges are dependent on a variety of factors, including qualifications, experience and geographic location. Range is not inclusive of potential equity offering, bonus or benefits. Your recruiter can share more information about the salary range specific to your working location and other factors during the hiring process.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":4038190002,"name":"Executive","child_ids":[4047184002,4048791002,4053407002,4047188002,4112306002,4047190002,4053405002,4055377002,4047189002,4047185002,4065652002,4081661002,4047187002,4047191002,4053408002,4056422002,4051163002,4053406002,4047186002],"parent_id":null}],"offices":[{"id":4000998002,"name":"San Francisco Office","location":"San Francisco, California, United States","child_ids":[],"parent_id":4031979002}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":null,"ai_opt_out_request_url":null},{"absolute_url":"https://app.careerpuck.com/job-board/lyft/job/8894912002?gh_jid=8894912002","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"education":"education_optional","employment":"employment_required","internal_job_id":6562649002,"location":{"name":"Toronto, Canada"},"metadata":[{"id":4345907002,"name":"Career Site Category","value":"Software Engineering","value_type":"single_select"}],"id":8894912002,"updated_at":"2026-10-19T18:43:36-04:00","requisition_id":"111263","title":"Engineering Manager, Dynamic Pricing","company_name":"Lyft","first_published":"2026-10-19T02:58:47-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;At Lyft, our purpose is to serve and connect. We aim to achieve this by cultivating a work environment where all team members belong and have the opportunity to thrive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Marketplace organization at Lyft is responsible for accelerating the growth of the business while delivering on key business and financial metrics, and Pricing sits at the heart of it. The Dynamic Pricing &amp;amp; Offer Selection team uses real-time and historical data to set the price of every ride on Lyft, balancing price and ETA so riders have a great experience and drivers have earning opportunities when and where demand is highest. We also decide which ride options a rider sees, which makes our systems one of the highest-traffic, most business-critical services at the company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re a tightly integrated team of software engineers and data scientists spread across the US and Canada. Engineers and scientists work side by side to take machine learning and optimization models from research to production while scaling our systems to handle more volume. We are looking for an Engineering Manager to lead a group of 6-8 engineers. You&#39;ll own the reliability and evolution of dynamic pricing systems that operate at Lyft&#39;s full scale, partner closely with our technical and product leadership to define the roadmap, and grow a strong team of engineers. This is a hands-on leadership role for someone who enjoys going deep on technical tradeoffs, cares equally about operational excellence and business outcomes, and is energized by working in a fast-paced environment with high impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Execution and Planning&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and drive engineering execution for the team&#39;s roadmap, from planning through delivery, adapting as priorities and business conditions change&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the team&#39;s engineering vision and short- and mid-term plans in partnership with Science and Product, making clear tradeoffs between technology, product and business needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate cross-functional decision-making and resolve blockers with partner teams across Marketplace&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build relationships with key stakeholders to align on standards, identify collaboration opportunities, and keep them informed of risks and dependencies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Technical Leadership&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand the team&#39;s stack deeply and be accountable for architectural decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with tech leads and scientists to productionize models safely, with strong experimentation, shadowing, rollout and monitoring practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure production readiness by setting success metrics, SLAs and reliability standards; own on-call health and serve as an escalation point during incidents, including major events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage tech debt and make sure systems stay reliable, efficient and cost-effective as the platform evolves&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;People&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire, develop and retain a diverse team of engineers, and build an environment where open, positive collaboration between engineering and science is the norm&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set clear expectations, give timely feedback, evaluate performance fairly, and support each engineer&#39;s growth and career development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Match people to opportunities that stretch them, and develop future technical leaders on the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and refine team processes, tooling and operating rhythms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the broader Lyft engineering community through mentoring, interviewing and knowledge sharing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B.S. or M.S. in Computer Science or equivalent practical experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 5 years of software development experience, with enough technical depth to engage credibly in architecture and design discussions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 3 years of people management experience, with a demonstrated ability to grow engineers and build cohesive teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of delivering projects end-to-end in a fast-paced environment, balancing speed with quality and sustainability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong cross-functional collaboration skills — comfortable working alongside Product, Design, Science, and Analytics to align on priorities and drive shared outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate effectively in ambiguity, decompose complex problems, and bring structure and clarity to the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing a diverse set of engineering roles — backend, web, mobile, and/or data — is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on a growth-focused team or org (incentives, messaging, ads) is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to represent the team clearly to senior stakeholders and advocate effectively for resourcing and prioritization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extended health and dental coverage options, along with life insurance and disability benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health benefits&lt;/li&gt;
