&lt;p&gt;Lyft is looking for a Legislative Counsel to join our fast-growing and fast-paced team. Based in Washington D.C this stellar individual will be directly involved in shaping the policy framework for the evolving ridesharing industry as a pivotal part of our Public Policy team.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide legal expertise to Lyft’s Public Policy team on legislative issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track, analyze, and evaluate proposed legislation across topic areas, identifying risks and opportunities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft legislative language, amendments, and recommendations that reflect the interests of Lyft’s users and business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify legislative trends and develop responsive strategies across subject matters and jurisdictions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate cross-functionally to assess legislative impacts and inform decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Lyft’s regional Public Policy team members on market-specific legislative efforts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop leading expertise on a specific issue area, in coordination with their manager.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with Lyft’s compliance, legal, and operations teams as new regulatory frameworks are implemented.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Law degree required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience with legislative drafting for a local, state and/or federal legislative body, or at a trade association or company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional ability to critically analyze policy and legal issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills and attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to thrive in a fast-paced, demanding (and sometimes unstructured) environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-starter; intrinsically motivated.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with insurance, transportation, technology, AI, privacy, or labor and employment law a plus but not required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Great medical, dental, and vision insurance options with additional programs available when enrolled&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family building benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Child care and pet benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) plan with company match to help save for your future&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In addition to 12 observed holidays, salaried team members have discretionary paid time off, hourly team members have 15 days paid time off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;18 weeks of paid parental leave. Biological, adoptive, and foster parents are all eligible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subsidized commuter benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly Lyft credits and complimentary Lyft Pink membership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lyft is an equal opportunity employer committed to an inclusive workplace that fosters belonging. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regards to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, age, genetic information, or any other basis prohibited by law. We also consider qualified applicants with criminal histories consistent with applicable federal, state and local law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lyft highly values having employees working in-office to foster a collaborative work environment and company culture. This role will be in-office on a hybrid schedule — Team Members will be expected to work in the office 3 days per week on Mondays, Wednesdays, and Thursdays. Lyft considers working in the office at least 3 days per week to be an essential function of this hybrid role. Your recruiter can share more information about the various in-office perks Lyft offers. Additionally, hybrid roles have the flexibility to work from anywhere for up to 4 weeks per year. #Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The expected base pay range for this position in the Washington D.C. area is $118,000 - $147,500, not inclusive of potential equity offering, bonus or benefits. Salary ranges are dependent on a variety of factors, including qualifications, experience and geographic location. Your recruiter can share more information about the salary range specific to your working location and other factors during the hiring process.&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":4082067002,"name":"Policy Development","child_ids":[],"parent_id":4002295002}],"offices":[{"id":4001015002,"name":"D.C. Office","location":"Washington, District of Columbia, United States","child_ids":[],"parent_id":4032267002}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":null,"ai_opt_out_request_url":null},{"absolute_url":"https://app.careerpuck.com/job-board/lyft/job/8779925002?gh_jid=8779925002","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"education":"education_optional","employment":"employment_required","internal_job_id":6512298002,"location":{"name":"Longueuil, Canada"},"metadata":[{"id":4345907002,"name":"Career Site Category","value":"Hardware Engineering","value_type":"single_select"}],"id":8779925002,"updated_at":"2026-10-19T18:43:36-04:00","requisition_id":"111143","title":"Manufacturing Test Engineer, Lyft Urban Solutions","company_name":"Lyft","first_published":"2026-09-03T10:40:15-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;At Lyft, our purpose is to serve and connect. We aim to achieve this by cultivating a work environment where all team members belong and have the opportunity to thrive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lyft Urban Solutions powers the bike-sharing and scooter-sharing systems that move millions of people in over 60 cities worldwide. We built North America&#39;s first automated bike-share system and continue to lead the micromobility revolution. Our systems operate globally - from Citi Bike in New York to BIXI in Montreal, Divvy in Chicago, Capital Bikeshare in DC, and iconic systems in Austin, Barcelona, Bogota, Boston, Buenos Aires, Columbus, Detroit, Dubai, London, Madrid, Mexico City, Monaco, Pittsburgh, Portland, Rio de Janeiro, San Francisco, Toronto, and beyond.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re not just technology providers - we operate these systems, building the software, hardware, and operations that make urban micromobility work at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ready to shape how millions of people move through their cities every day?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our team is transforming urban transportation through Lyft’s micromobility ecosystem — the shared bikes and scooters riders use every day.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lyft’s Hardware Manufacturing &amp;amp; Quality team is looking for a Manufacturing Test Engineer to design, build, and manage the test systems that ensure every bike and scooter leaving our production lines is safe, durable, and functional. You’ll own the software, electrical, and hardware test fixtures used on the factory floor, and you’ll be the person production turns to when something breaks — whether that’s a failing assembly or a misbehaving test station.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Test System Ownership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and own the software, electrical, and hardware test fixtures used during production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the vision, strategy, and architecture for current and future manufacturing test systems, and author the test specifications and fixture acceptance plans that govern quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write scripts and programs to run automated tests and capture factory data for traceability and yield analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement features and tooling to support hardware testing across the product line&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own our in-house test platform: an OpenHTF-based Python execution runtime with YAML-driven config, product variants, and feature flags&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain the TypeScript/Electron/React operator application that communicates with the Python test agent over gRPC/protobuf&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage CI, signed installers, semver releases, and an S3-based auto-update pipeline with rollback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hardware Bring-Up &amp;amp; Validation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own firmware bring-up, validation, and testing of electronic PCBAs and multi-component electrical systems, including motor controllers, battery management systems, and vehicle-controller units&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Validate mechanical and electrical assemblies to confirm they meet safety, durability, and functional requirements before they ship&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Validate and troubleshoot factory tests, set factory test requirements, assist in software bring-up, and review test fixture software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Production &amp;amp; Factory Floor Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the eyes and ears on the ground in a manufacturing environment, partnering with engineers to triage issues, perform initial failure analysis, and drive corrective actions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot assembly failures on the production line and diagnose/fix bugs in test stations to keep the line running&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel on-site to contract manufacturers as needed to ensure designs are built and tested successfully&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional &amp;amp; Vendor Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally with contract manufacturers, supplier quality, and program teams to resolve manufacturing issues quickly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain key relationships with manufacturing partner teams, internal and external test/lab resources, and mechanical, electrical, and manufacturing engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage external fixture vendors, including design reviews and Factory/Site Acceptance Testing (FAT/SAT)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare concise, detailed design investigation summaries and test reports, and communicate cross-functionally to deliver successful products to market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate manufacturing requirements into terms enterprise IT and security teams can evaluate and support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead large test-engineering projects from concept through production execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A degree in Electrical Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Computer Engineering, Computer Science, or a related technical field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Python, C/C++, OpenHTF,TypeScript, or other scripting languages for test automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of hardware test equipment (DMMs, oscilloscopes, logic analyzers, custom test fixtures) and lab tools such as soldering and data acquisition&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Test fixture and station design and build.&lt;/strong&gt; You have designed a functional test station and physically built it — instrument selection, DUT interfacing and harnessing, PLC control and power sequencing, enclosure and panel work, BOM specification and procurement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with prototype bring-up and debugging, functional verification, and manufacturing support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with embedded systems design and communication protocols (CAN, USB, SPI, I2C, UART)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with ARM-based microcontrollers and RTOS frameworks, preferably the STM32 family.Firmware programming and recovery experience (e.g., ST-LINK/STM32, AVR/ISP, bootloaders)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong troubleshooting instincts and comfort working directly on the factory floor&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with hardware test frameworks (e.g., OpenHTF,TypeScript, React, Electron, gRPC, protobuf, and SQLite) or building test platforms from scratch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to MES/ERP integration experience, including traveler, BOM, and label generation (ZPL/Zebra).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to Cloud data plumbing experience (S3, Lambda/SQS) and dashboarding in Grafana or Mode&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to contract manufacturer (CM) relationships and global production ramps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with test data pipelines, traceability, or genealogy systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with firmware debug tools, serial consoles, JTAG/SWD adapters, and bootloaders to support hardware validation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Android or embedded Linux environments, including building, deploying, and debugging&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel to and work on-site at manufacturing and assembly vendors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extended health and dental coverage options, along with life insurance and disability benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family building benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pet benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to a Lyft funded Health Care Savings Account&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;RRSP plan with company match to help save for your future&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In addition to provincial observed holidays, salaried team members are covered under Lyft&#39;s flexible paid time off policy. The policy allows team members to take off as much time as they need (with manager approval). Hourly team members get 15 days paid time off, with an additional day for each year of service&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lyft is proud to support new parents with 18 weeks of paid time off, designed as a top-up plan to complement provincial programs. Biological, adoptive, and foster parents are all eligible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subsidized commuter benefits and Lyft ride credits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lyft is committed to creating an inclusive workforce that fosters belonging. Lyft believes that every person has a right to equal employment opportunities without discrimination because of race, ancestry, place of origin, colour, ethnic origin, citizenship, creed, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, marital status, family status, disability, pardoned record of offences, or any other basis protected by applicable law or by Company policy. Lyft also strives for a healthy and safe workplace and strictly prohibits harassment of any kind.&amp;nbsp; Accommodation for persons with disabilities will be provided upon request in accordance with applicable law during the application and hiring process. Please contact your recruiter if you wish to make such a request.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The expected base pay range for this position in the Montréal area is CAD $112,000 - CAD 140,000, not inclusive of potential equity offering, bonus or benefits. Salary ranges are dependent on a variety of factors, including qualifications, experience and geographic location. Your recruiter can share more information about the salary range specific to your working location and other factors during the hiring process.&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":4056716002,"name":"LUS Hardware","child_ids":[],"parent_id":4008519002}],"offices":[{"id":4038242002,"name":"Montreal Office","location":"Montreal, Canada, Montreal","child_ids":[],"parent_id":4038337002}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":null,"ai_opt_out_request_url":null},{"absolute_url":"https://app.careerpuck.com/job-board/lyft/job/8780046002?gh_jid=8780046002","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"education":"education_optional","employment":"employment_required","internal_job_id":6512353002,"location":{"name":"Toronto, Canada"},"metadata":[{"id":4345907002,"name":"Career Site Category","value":"Information Technology","value_type":"single_select"}],"id":8780046002,"updated_at":"2026-10-19T18:43:36-04:00","requisition_id":"111145","title":"Marketing Technology Lead","company_name":"Lyft","first_published":"2026-09-03T12:39:56-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;At Lyft, our purpose is to serve and connect. We aim to achieve this by cultivating a work environment where all team members belong and have the opportunity to thrive.&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are hiring a Marketing Technology Lead to own Lyft&#39;s B2B marketing technology stack, spanning marketing automation, content and web, lead routing, data enrichment, and attribution. As the senior technical owner of that stack, you will lead solution design, own the architecture and data model that carry a lead from first touch through to a qualified opportunity, and partner with Marketing Operations, Sales Operations, Sales Technology, Privacy, Legal, and Data to translate business needs into durable, scalable systems. This is a hands-on leadership role for someone who knows B2B marketing operations, can build the systems that run them, and is looking for ways to bring AI into how the stack works, not just what it produces.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the senior technical owner of the B2B marketing technology stack, from solution design through delivery, adoption, and ongoing support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead requirements gathering with Marketing Operations, Sales Operations, Sales Technology, and Data partners, and translate them into functional and technical designs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remain hands-on, configuring and extending the marketing automation platform (HubSpot) across workflows, forms, lead scoring, and custom objects, and building the integrations that connect the stack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the marketing technology roadmap and architecture, including the lead and account data model, enrichment and routing logic, and integrations with the CRM, data platform, web, and advertising systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the tracking and instrumentation layer, including tag management, site and campaign tracking, and the data capture behind attribution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the lead lifecycle systems, partnering with Sales Operations and Sales Technology on lead identity, deduplication, scoring, routing, MQL and SQL definitions, and funnel stage integrity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify where AI can improve the stack, from lead scoring and routing to content and campaign workflows, and lead the evaluation, adoption, and rollout of those capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess the stack against target state and introduce new tools as the marketing motion matures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the technical standard through design review and documentation that accounts for failure states, scalability, and supportability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain platform reliability by monitoring performance and email deliverability, supporting incident resolution, leading postmortems, and driving automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own governance and controls for marketing data, including consent and subscription management, email and privacy compliance, data quality, and change management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the marketing tool portfolio and budget, from evaluation and selection through procurement, contracting, and renewals, partnering with Procurement, Legal, and Security.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the technical expert and escalation point, and deliver technical enablement to partner teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with marketing leaders on prioritization, mentor the engineers and contractors supporting the stack, and support hiring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate marketing technology strategy, roadmap, and vision to partner teams, and give senior leadership decision-ready updates on progress, risks, and tradeoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Business, Information Systems, Computer Science, or a related field, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in a marketing technology, marketing operations engineering, or business systems role, including 3+ years leading solution design and delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of hands-on administration and configuration of a B2B marketing automation platform (HubSpot, Marketo, Pardot, or Eloqua), with at least one active platform certification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on depth in at least two platform categories beyond marketing automation, such as content management, lead routing, data enrichment, ABM, analytics, or attribution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years hands-on in Salesforce or an equivalent CRM, and 3 or more delivered integrations to systems such as a data warehouse or CMS using REST APIs, webhooks, or middleware.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with tag management and web or campaign tracking instrumentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Led end-to-end delivery of at least 2 large, cross-functional marketing technology programs, including one platform implementation or migration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience providing technical direction to engineers, contractors, or implementation partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of B2B demand generation and lead-to-opportunity workflows, including lead scoring, routing, attribution, and funnel reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to communicate technical direction and tradeoffs to non-technical stakeholders, and present roadmap and status to senior leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with marketing data quality, consent and subscription management, and email and privacy compliance (CAN-SPAM, CASL, GDPR, or equivalent) is highly desirable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with a cloud data platform such as Databricks or Snowflake, and with SQL, is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extended health and dental coverage options, along with life insurance and disability benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family building benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Child care and pet benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to a Lyft funded Health Care Savings Account&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;RRSP plan with company match to help save for your future&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In addition to provincial observed holidays, salaried team members are covered under Lyft&#39;s flexible paid time off policy. The policy allows team members to take off as much time as they need (with manager approval). Hourly team members get 15 days paid time off, with an additional day for each year of service&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lyft is proud to support new parents with 18 weeks of paid time off, designed as a top-up plan to complement provincial programs. Biological, adoptive, and foster parents are all eligible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subsidized commuter benefits and Lyft ride credits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Lyft is committed to creating an inclusive workforce that fosters belonging. Lyft believes that every person has a right to equal employment opportunities without discrimination because of race, ancestry, place of origin, colour, ethnic origin, citizenship, creed, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, marital status, family status, disability, pardoned record of offences, or any other basis protected by applicable law or by Company policy. Lyft also strives for a healthy and safe workplace and strictly prohibits harassment of any kind.&amp;nbsp; Accommodation for persons with disabilities will be provided upon request in accordance with applicable law during the application and hiring process. Please contact your recruiter if you wish to make such a request.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Lyft highly values having employees working in-office to foster a collaborative work environment and company culture. &lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;This role will be in-office on a hybrid schedule — Team Members will be expected to work in the office at least 3 days per week, including on Mondays, Wednesdays, and Thursdays. &lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Lyft considers working in the office at least 3 days per week to be an essential function of this hybrid role. Your recruiter can share more information about the various in-office perks Lyft offers. &lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Additionally, hybrid roles have the flexibility to work from anywhere for up to 4 weeks per year. &lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;#Hybrid&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The expected base pay range for this position in the Toronto area is $129,000-$161,250, not inclusive of potential equity offering, bonus or benefits. Salary ranges are dependent on a variety of factors, including qualifications, experience and geographic location. Your recruiter can share more information about the salary range specific to your working location and other factors during the hiring process.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Lyft may use artificial intelligence to screen applicants, however, Lyft employees make the ultimate selection and hiring decisions.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This is a new position.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":4135509002,"name":"Foundations & AI Transformation","child_ids":[4135510002,4082084002,4054368002,4005746002,4002287002,4030548002],"parent_id":4042810002}],"offices":[{"id":4080790002,"name":"Toronto Coworking","location":"Toronto, Ontario, Canada","child_ids":[],"parent_id":4038336002}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":null,"ai_opt_out_request_url":null},{"absolute_url":"https://app.careerpuck.com/job-board/lyft/job/8639200002?gh_jid=8639200002","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"education":"education_optional","employment":"employment_required","internal_job_id":6450365002,"location":{"name":"San Francisco, CA"},"metadata":[{"id":4345907002,"name":"Career Site Category","value":"Software Engineering","value_type":"single_select"}],"id":8639200002,"updated_at":"2026-10-19T18:43:36-04:00","requisition_id":"111002","title":"ML Software Engineer, ETA","company_name":"Lyft","first_published":"2026-07-20T16:55:30-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;At Lyft, our purpose is to serve and connect. We aim to achieve this by cultivating a work environment where all team members belong and have the opportunity to thrive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are hiring a Machine Learning Engineer to join our ETA team. Our team builds and maintains Lyft&#39;s system responsible for estimating/predicting ETAs for every ride request on our platform. ETAs play a critical role in matching decisions, pricing estimates and overall user experience. Low latency, high reliability and high accuracy are paramount for our success.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are a critical thinker with experience in machine learning workflows and writing reliable code, passionate about solving business problems using data and working in a dynamic, creative, and collaborative environment, we are searching for you.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our technology stack runs on AWS, Kubernetes, Go, Spark, Python and Apache Airflow. In this role, you will work with incredibly passionate and talented colleagues from software engineering, machine learning and data science on building rideshare experiences that delight millions of riders and drivers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform data analysis and build proof-of-concept to explore and compare ML and non-ML solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be able to make effective tradeoffs between model accuracy, its productization complexity and runtime performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop statistical, machine learning, or optimization models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write production quality code that can scale well to serve millions of requests per day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in code reviews, design reviews, production on-call support and incident triaging process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write well-crafted, well-tested, readable, maintainable code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B.S., M.S., or Ph.D. in Computer Science or other quantitative fields or related work experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of Machine Learning experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Nice-to-have: Experience with big data processing / distributed data pipelines and tools such as Apache Airflow and Spark&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in distributed teams spread across time zones. (North America and Europe)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
