&lt;p&gt;Flexdrive is a subsidiary of Lyft that works together with Lyft teams to realize our shared mission.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Flexdrive builds the operational backbone for the future of mobility. As a leader in fleet management and a Lyft subsidiary, we&#39;re extending our expertise into autonomous vehicle (AV) infrastructure — managing the physical operations that keep AV fleets safe, available, and performing at scale. Our Nashville depot is the first proof point in a multi-market expansion, and we&#39;re building the leadership team to sustain and scale it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the &lt;strong&gt;Senior Manager, AV Operations&lt;/strong&gt; you&#39;ll be instrumental in &lt;strong&gt;owning and evolving the operational playbooks&lt;/strong&gt; for our AV operations. You&#39;ll act as the &lt;strong&gt;primary operational leader&lt;/strong&gt;, responsible for creating the strategic framework, executing complex projects, and ensuring the seamless functioning of our AV support infrastructure in close partnership with our AV technology partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is for a&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;hands-on leader&lt;/strong&gt; with a unique blend of strategic foresight, project management excellence, and deep operational knowledge within the AV or complex fleet management space. If you thrive in ambiguous environments, are adept at building from the ground up, and possess the business acumen to drive efficiency and scalability, enabling our AV operations to thrive, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Execution &amp;amp; Site Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Daily Operational Execution:&lt;/strong&gt;Lead the day-to-day execution of critical operational systems and processes for our 24/7 AV fleet management operations, including depot layout adherence, vehicle flow (charging, cleaning, maintenance, staging, diagnostics), parts management, and data handling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational Resource Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Manage operational resources (equipment, technology, consumables, staffing) efficiently on a daily basis to ensure maximum uptime and operational readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technology Utilization:&lt;/strong&gt; Execute operational procedures using necessary technologies and tools to enable efficient AV operations within the depot environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational Excellence &amp;amp; Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Site Leadership: &lt;/strong&gt;Serve as the primary operational head for the AV depot, driving daily performance, hands-on problem-solving, and ensuring adherence to all operational and safety protocols.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance Monitoring &amp;amp; Optimization: &lt;/strong&gt;Monitor key performance indicators (KPIs) for depot operations (e.g., vehicle uptime, turnaround time, maintenance efficiency, cost per vehicle) and swiftly address operational bottlenecks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process Execution &amp;amp; Refinement: &lt;/strong&gt;Execute Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs), Service Level Agreements (SLAs), and safety protocols for all aspects of AV fleet management within the depot environment. Identify practical improvements and roll them out to the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Floor Presence:&lt;/strong&gt; Maintain a strong floor presence, leading by example and directly supporting the team during peak operational periods or complex troubleshooting events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder, Partner &amp;amp; Team Collaboration&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Management &amp;amp; Enablement:&lt;/strong&gt; Manage the AV operators and technicians, handling scheduling, performance management, training, and fostering a positive, safety-first culture on the shop floor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner Relationship Management: &lt;/strong&gt;Work closely with our AV technology partners on the ground, ensuring their operational needs are met and collaborating on joint initiatives for fleet health and performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vendor Execution&lt;/strong&gt;: Oversee daily interactions with external vendors and partners for equipment, services, and facility needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regulatory &amp;amp; Compliance:&lt;/strong&gt; Enforce all operations guidelines to adhere to local, state, and federal regulations for autonomous vehicles, commercial fleet management, and workplace safety.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of progressive experience in site management, general management, or operational leadership, with a strong understanding of complex fleet management, logistics, or autonomous vehicle (AV) operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of managing established operational sites, with a focus on executing playbooks, driving daily efficiency, and managing physical infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ability to work a flexible schedule, including nights, weekends, and holidays as needed, to effectively support and lead a 24/7 AV depot operation.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional people management skills, including proficiency in shift scheduling, performance management, and building a strong safety and operational culture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly analytical and practical mindset, capable of interpreting daily performance data to drive immediate improvements in efficiency and productivity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated leadership ability in fast-paced operational environments, with excellent communication and interpersonal skills to lead on-site teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Engineering, Business, Operations Management, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Great medical, dental, and vision insurance options with additional programs available when enrolled&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family building benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Child care and pet benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) plan with company match to help save for your future&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In addition to 12 observed holidays, salaried team members have discretionary paid time off, hourly team members have 15 days paid time off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;18 weeks of paid parental leave. Biological, adoptive, and foster parents are all eligible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subsidized commuter benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly Lyft credits and complimentary Lyft Pink membership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;: For this role, candidates must reside in states registered for Flexdrive Services LLC.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This role is on-site at a Lyft Flexdrive hub or office location full time. &lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;#Onsite&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The expected base pay range for this position in the Nashville area is $108,240 - $135,300, not inclusive of potential equity offering, bonus or benefits. Salary ranges are dependent on a variety of factors, including qualifications, experience and geographic location. Your recruiter can share more information about the salary range specific to your working location and other factors during the hiring process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Flexdrive is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to an inclusive workplace that fosters belonging. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regards to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, age, genetic information, or any other basis prohibited by law. Flexdrive also strives for a healthy and safe workplace and strictly prohibits harassment of any kind. Flexdrive will also consider employment for qualified applicants with criminal histories consistent with applicable federal, state and local law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":4135513002,"name":"AV & Fleet Operations","child_ids":[],"parent_id":4135512002}],"offices":[{"id":4118460002,"name":"Nashville AV Depot","location":"Nashville, Tennessee, Nashville","child_ids":[],"parent_id":4038194002}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":null,"ai_opt_out_request_url":null},{"absolute_url":"https://app.careerpuck.com/job-board/lyft/job/8689228002?gh_jid=8689228002","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"employment":"employment_required","internal_job_id":6471653002,"location":{"name":"Washington, DC"},"metadata":[{"id":4345907002,"name":"Career Site Category","value":"Operations","value_type":"single_select"}],"id":8689228002,"updated_at":"2026-10-19T18:43:36-04:00","requisition_id":"111068","title":"Operations Specialist, Capital Bikeshare","company_name":"Lyft","first_published":"2026-08-07T10:26:17-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;At Lyft, our purpose is to serve and connect. We aim to achieve this by cultivating a work environment where all team members belong and have the opportunity to thrive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lyft Urban Solutions powers the bike-sharing and scooter-sharing systems that move millions of people in over 60 cities worldwide. We built North America&#39;s first automated bike-share system and continue to lead the micromobility revolution. Our systems operate globally - from Citi Bike in New York to BIXI in Montreal, Divvy in Chicago, Capital Bikeshare in DC, and iconic systems in Austin, Barcelona, Bogota, Boston, Buenos Aires, Columbus, Detroit, Dubai, London, Madrid, Mexico City, Monaco, Pittsburgh, Portland, Rio de Janeiro, San Francisco, Toronto, and beyond.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re not just technology providers - we operate these systems, building the software, hardware, and operations that make urban micromobility work at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ready to shape how millions of people move through their cities every day?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lyft Urban Solutions is the operator of six bikeshare systems across the country, including &lt;a href=&quot;https://capitalbikeshare.com/&quot;&gt;Capital Bikeshare&lt;/a&gt;, the DMV’s public bike share system. We’re looking for an Operations Specialist who wants to continue the micromobility revolution.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Operations Specialist, you will support the General Manager of Capital Bikeshare developing and executing operational plans with a consistent eye towards service quality, operational excellence, continuous improvement, and the overall customer experience. You’ll roll up your sleeves for some hands-on problem solving, while also tackling big picture projects to improve the Capital Bikeshare system.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you share our vision for active transportation that empowers local communities, reduces our environmental footprint, and brings people together, then we’d love to meet you!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure smooth daily field operations: create/refine playbooks and SOPs, oversee aspects of contractor relationship management, and perform occasional quality checks in field and depot&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end processes like invoicing and asset tracking to support the success of the business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Audit performance of functional areas against SLAs, proactively identifying and escalating risks and inefficiencies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the Capital Bikeshare team in maintaining relationships with our city partners and addressing market-specific operational issues or special projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct deep-dive analysis to identify root causes of issues, using insights from field operations and data to collaborate with teams, implement solutions, and drive performance improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate clearly and confidently with stakeholders, clients, and vendors, tackling challenging conversations when necessary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage shifting priorities effectively, adapting to dynamic needs while maintaining a positive, solution-oriented attitude&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree or 4+ years of experience overseeing operations in a complex, fast-moving, rapidly changing environment such as a distribution warehouse, marketplace, or delivery operation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using Google Sheets and other data analysis tools to identify inefficiencies and propose solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent organizational and time management skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail, with an ability to zoom out and understand the bigger context of your work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of data-based problem-solving with the ability to think on your feet&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a warehouse or hands-on operations environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interest in biking, bikeshare, sustainable transportation, and city planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with AI tools to strengthen day-to-day productivity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Great medical, dental, and vision insurance options with additional programs available when enrolled&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family building benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Child care and pet benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) plan with company match to help save for your future&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In addition to 12 observed holidays, salaried team members have discretionary paid time off, hourly team members have 15 days paid time off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;18 weeks of paid parental leave. Biological, adoptive, and foster parents are all eligible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subsidized commuter benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly Lyft credits and complimentary Lyft Pink membership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lyft is an equal opportunity employer committed to an inclusive workplace that fosters belonging. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regards to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, age, genetic information, or any other basis prohibited by law. We also consider qualified applicants with criminal histories consistent with applicable federal, state and local law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lyft highly values having employees working in-office to foster a collaborative work environment and company culture. This role will be in-office on a hybrid schedule — Team Members will be expected to work in the office 3 days per week on Mondays, Wednesdays, and Thursdays. Lyft considers working in the office at least 3 days per week to be an essential function of this hybrid role. Your recruiter can share more information about the various in-office perks Lyft offers. Additionally, hybrid roles have the flexibility to work from anywhere for up to 4 weeks per year. #Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The expected base pay range for this position in the Washington D.C. area is $66,240 - $82,800 not inclusive of potential equity offering, bonus or benefits. Salary ranges are dependent on a variety of factors, including qualifications, experience and geographic location. Your recruiter can share more information about the salary range specific to your working location and other factors during the hiring process.&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":4094259002,"name":"LUS Bike Market Operations","child_ids":[],"parent_id":4008519002}],"offices":[{"id":4001015002,"name":"D.C. Office","location":"Washington, District of Columbia, United States","child_ids":[],"parent_id":4032267002}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":null,"ai_opt_out_request_url":null},{"absolute_url":"https://app.careerpuck.com/job-board/lyft/job/8611874002?gh_jid=8611874002","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"education":"education_optional","employment":"employment_required","internal_job_id":6439528002,"location":{"name":"Montreal, Canada"},"metadata":[{"id":4345907002,"name":"Career Site Category","value":"Design","value_type":"single_select"}],"id":8611874002,"updated_at":"2026-10-23T10:10:29-04:00","requisition_id":"110933","title":"Operations Technology Product Designer","company_name":"Lyft","first_published":"2026-08-03T13:59:24-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;At Lyft, our purpose is to serve and connect. We aim to achieve this by cultivating a work environment where all team members belong and have the opportunity to thrive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lyft Urban Solutions powers the bike-sharing and scooter-sharing systems that move millions of people in over 60 cities worldwide. We built North America&#39;s first automated bike-share system and continue to lead the micromobility revolution. Our systems operate globally - from Citi Bike in New York to BIXI in Montreal, Divvy in Chicago, Capital Bikeshare in DC, and iconic systems in Austin, Barcelona, Bogota, Boston, Buenos Aires, Columbus, Detroit, Dubai, London, Madrid, Mexico City, Monaco, Pittsburgh, Portland, Rio de Janeiro, San Francisco, Toronto, and beyond.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re not just technology providers - we operate these systems, building the software, hardware, and operations that make urban micromobility work at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ready to shape how millions of people move through their cities every day?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a passionate Product Designer to join our Montreal office to work on Lyft’s micromobility Operations Technology team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a member of the Operations Technology team, you’ll be responsible for evolving the platform that drives the global on-the-ground operations of our business. You’ll be designing features that are used in warehouses, vans, &amp;amp; on-the-ground to make our transportation systems some of the most reliable in the world. You’ll confront complex technical challenges &amp;amp; advocate for experiences that delight our operators and promote efficiency.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Montreal office developed the first automated bikes-share system in North America and continues to work on the platform today that provides state-of-the-art electric bikes and scooters for tens of millions of rides per year.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a product designer at Lyft, you will be involved at every step of product development, from brainstorming broad ideas to ensuring design quality through launch. Using your full range of interaction, visual, and product thinking skills. As a product designer on the Lyft Urban Solutions team you will own the design of features within the core rider experience for our bike and scooter riders, within the Lyft app and our market specific apps.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In a lot of ways, we function as a startup, meaning we all work closely and collaboratively across organizations to align on product vision and ship products. Our Design and Research teams live and breathe a user-centered process to create the best possible, end-to-end, experience for riders all over the world. We can be scrappy when we need to be, though we are always focused on quality and influence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a qualified candidate, you have a track record of leading projects to successful outcomes for users and the business. You are a strong cross-functional partner, a great communicator, and are able to take a solution from idea to implementation. You uphold a high-quality bar and have a strong appreciation for the details. Above all, you approach problems holistically and create elegantly simple solutions to multi-faceted problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Problem solve, think big, and explore divergent concepts/ideas while understanding how to converge and build iteratively towards your vision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan strategically and think tactically as a partner with product and engineering to define the future of the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence the shape of the product with research and data while executing design work using high quality wireframes, mockups, user journeys, and cross-platform interactive prototypes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advocate for design by sharing your work and presenting cross-functionally, while being able to precisely articulate design rationale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inspire the entire team (including your cross-functional) partners by bringing new ideas to the table.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create a unified, end-to-end experience through close collaboration with team members from across the Product and Marketing Design Teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience working in UX, UI, HCI related field with experience working on web and mobile design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with a lean team of Engineers, Product Managers and Program Managers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing innovative products for desktop and mobile&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent oral and written communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with user research methods and analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise with Figma and other prototyping tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellence in design craft&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work with a low-ego, highly collaborative, cross-functional team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excited about working in a fast-paced, dynamic startup environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Even if you don&#39;t directly have the skills above, please consider applying. We know talent takes many different shapes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extended health and dental coverage options, along with life insurance and disability benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family building benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pet benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to a Lyft funded Health Care Savings Account&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;RRSP plan with company match to help save for your future&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In addition to provincial observed holidays, salaried team members are covered under Lyft&#39;s flexible paid time off policy. The policy allows team members to take off as much time as they need (with manager approval). Hourly team members get 15 days paid time off, with an additional day for each year of service&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lyft is proud to support new parents with 18 weeks of paid time off, designed as a top-up plan to complement provincial programs. Biological, adoptive, and foster parents are all eligible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subsidized commuter benefits and Lyft ride credits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lyft is committed to creating an inclusive workforce that fosters belonging. Lyft believes that every person has a right to equal employment opportunities without discrimination because of race, ancestry, place of origin, colour, ethnic origin, citizenship, creed, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, marital status, family status, disability, pardoned record of offences, or any other basis protected by applicable law or by Company policy. Lyft also strives for a healthy and safe workplace and strictly prohibits harassment of any kind.&amp;nbsp; Accommodation for persons with disabilities will be provided upon request in accordance with applicable law during the application and hiring process. Please contact your recruiter if you wish to make such a request.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lyft highly values having employees working in-office to foster a collaborative work environment and company culture. This role will be in-office on a hybrid schedule — Team Members will be expected to work in the office at least 3 days per week, including on Mondays, Wednesdays, and Thursdays. Lyft considers working in the office at least 3 days per week to be an essential function of this hybrid role. Your recruiter can share more information about the various in-office perks Lyft offers. Additionally, hybrid roles have the flexibility to work from anywhere for up to 4 weeks per year. #Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The expected base pay range for this position in the Montreal area is CAD $88,000 - CAD $110,000, not inclusive of potential equity offering, bonus or benefits. Salary ranges are dependent on a variety of factors, including qualifications, experience and geographic location. Your recruiter can share more information about the salary range specific to your working location and other factors during the hiring process.&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":4092660002,"name":"LUS Supply & Operations Technology","child_ids":[],"parent_id":4008519002}],"offices":[{"id":4038242002,"name":"Montreal Office","location":"Montreal, Canada, Montreal","child_ids":[],"parent_id":4038337002}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":null,"ai_opt_out_request_url":null},{"absolute_url":"https://app.careerpuck.com/job-board/lyft/job/8872198002?gh_jid=8872198002","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"education":"education_optional","employment":"employment_required","internal_job_id":6552537002,"location":{"name":"Montreal, Canada"},"metadata":[{"id":4345907002,"name":"Career Site Category","value":"People","value_type":"single_select"}],"id":8872198002,"updated_at":"2026-10-19T18:43:36-04:00","requisition_id":"111245","title":"Partenaire d’affaires RH, Lyft Solutions Urbaines","company_name":"Lyft","first_published":"2026-10-06T16:44:20-04:00","language":"fr","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;Chez Lyft, notre mission est de servir et de connecter. Nous y parvenons en favorisant un environnement de travail où chacun trouve sa place et a la possibilité de s&#39;épanouir.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lyft Solutions Urbaines (souvent appelé LUS) crée des programmes de vélopartage que les usagers adorent, dont les villes ont besoin et que les exploitants apprécient. Nous concevons, fabriquons et soutenons les vélos et la technologie des stations qui font fonctionner des programmes de vélopartage dans des villes du monde entier, dont BIXI. Notre équipe de Montréal est au cœur de ce travail : elle réunit sous un même toit les équipes d&#39;ingénierie, de fabrication, de chaîne d&#39;approvisionnement, d&#39;opérations, de marketing et commerciales.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;À titre de partenaire d&#39;affaires RH pour LUS, vous serez la personne-ressource de référence en matière de gestion des personnes et agirez également comme principal responsable RH du site de Montréal. Vous traduirez les priorités d&#39;affaires en plans RH concrets, aiderez les gestionnaires à composer avec des enjeux humains complexes et veillerez à ce que nos programmes soient bien adaptés au contexte québécois. Vous relèverez du partenaire d&#39;affaires RH principal de notre équipe Global Growth et travaillerez en étroite collaboration avec les équipes Relations avec les employés, Rémunération globale, Acquisition de talents, Opérations RH et Affaires juridiques.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Il s&#39;agit d&#39;un rôle très opérationnel pour une personne qui aime être proche des activités. Pour réussir, vous devrez bien comprendre les objectifs, les indicateurs, la performance et les opportunités de l&#39;équipe afin d&#39;élaborer des stratégies RH qui les soutiennent. Vous êtes tout aussi à l&#39;aise d&#39;accompagner un nouveau gestionnaire dans une conversation difficile que d&#39;aider un directeur à réfléchir à la structure de son équipe pour l&#39;année à venir.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsabilités:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Agir comme partenaire auprès des gestionnaires et des leaders de LUS sur la santé des équipes, la performance, le développement et la rétention, en offrant un accompagnement stratégique direct, pragmatique et ancré dans la réalité des affaires.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assumer les responsabilités RH du site de Montréal, notamment les liens avec la CNESST et l&#39;OQLF, ainsi que la gestion du programme lié à la Loi favorisant le développement et la reconnaissance des compétences de la main-d&#39;œuvre (loi du 1 %).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gérer de façon autonome et avec rigueur les cycles RH : mettre en œuvre les évaluations de rendement, les cycles de rémunération, les revues de talents, la planification de la main-d&#39;œuvre, les rapports sur la santé organisationnelle et les sondages d&#39;engagement pour vos groupes clients, en vous assurant que les gestionnaires sont prêts pour chacun d&#39;eux.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Soutenir les dossiers de relations de travail avec bienveillance et discernement, de la première conversation jusqu&#39;à la résolution, en collaboration avec les équipes Relations avec les employés et Affaires juridiques pour les dossiers complexes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Soutenir les changements organisationnels, qu&#39;il s&#39;agisse de petites restructurations d&#39;équipe ou de transformations plus importantes de l&#39;organisation de LUS, y compris la planification, la préparation des gestionnaires, la gestion de projet et la communication auprès des membres de l&#39;équipe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Appliquer le droit et les pratiques du travail du Québec aux programmes mondiaux de Lyft, et signaler rapidement tout élément nécessitant une adaptation locale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utiliser les données pour dégager des tendances (roulement, engagement, embauche, etc.) et les présenter aux leaders avec une recommandation claire sur les prochaines étapes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborer avec l&#39;équipe Finances pour suivre les coûts liés aux effectifs, responsabiliser les leaders et les conseiller sur les ajustements d&#39;effectifs afin de respecter le budget tout en optimisant les résultats d&#39;affaires.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assurer une présence visible et de confiance sur le site, particulièrement auprès des équipes qui ne travaillent pas derrière un bureau.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Expérience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Au moins 5 ans d&#39;expérience en RH, dont au moins 2 à 3 ans dans un rôle de partenaire d&#39;affaires RH ou de conseiller RH généraliste soutenant directement des gestionnaires.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connaissance pratique du droit du travail québécois et expérience de son application.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maîtrise professionnelle du français et de l&#39;anglais, à l&#39;écrit comme à l&#39;oral.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solide expérience en gestion des relations de travail, notamment les enquêtes, la gestion du rendement et les fins d&#39;emploi.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expérience auprès d&#39;employés salariés de bureau et de personnel payé à l&#39;heure, de première ligne ou travaillant sur site.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expérience dans une entreprise en période d&#39;intégration, de restructuration ou de forte croissance, un atout.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Aisance avec les systèmes RH (Workday ou équivalent) et avec l&#39;utilisation des données pour appuyer des recommandations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Avantages:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellente couverture d’assurance santé, dentaire, vision, ainsi que l’assurance vie et prestation d’invalidité&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Programme de soutien en santé mentale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Soutien à la fertilité et à la planification familiale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Avantage pour les soins d&#39;animaux de compagnie&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compte de dépenses de santé (HSA)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Options de cotisation pour le REER&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;En plus des jours fériés observés dans la province, les membres salariés de l’équipe sont couverts par la politique flexible de congés payés de Lyft. La politique permet aux membres de l’équipe de prendre autant de temps qu’ils en ont besoin (avec l’approbation du gestionnaire). Les membres de l’équipe payés à l’heure bénéficient de 15 jours de congés payés, avec un jour supplémentaire pour chaque année de service&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lyft est fier de soutenir les nouveaux parents avec 18 semaines de congés payés, conçu comme une complémentarité aux programmes gouvernementaux. Les parents biologiques, adoptifs et adoptifs sont tous élus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Avantage lié au transport&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lyft s&#39;engage à créer un environnement de travail inclusif qui favorise l&#39;appartenance. Lyft estime que chaque personne a droit à l&#39;égalité des chances en matière d&#39;emploi, sans discrimination fondée sur la race, l&#39;ascendance, le lieu d&#39;origine, la couleur, l&#39;origine ethnique, la citoyenneté, les croyances, le sexe, l&#39;orientation sexuelle, l&#39;identité de genre, l&#39;expression de genre, l&#39;âge, l&#39;état matrimonial, la situation familiale, le handicap, l&#39;existence d&#39;un casier judiciaire gracié ou tout autre motif protégé par la loi applicable ou par la politique de l&#39;entreprise. Lyft s&#39;efforce également de créer un lieu de travail sain et sûr et interdit strictement tout harcèlement. Des aménagements pour les personnes handicapées seront fournis sur demande, conformément à la loi applicable, lors du processus de candidature et d&#39;embauche. Veuillez contacter votre recruteur si vous souhaitez faire une telle demande.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ce poste sera en présentiel selon un calendrier hybride - les membres de l&#39;équipe devront travailler au bureau 3 jours par semaine, les lundis, mercredis et jeudis. De plus, les postes hybrides offrent la flexibilité de travailler de n&#39;importe où pendant un maximum de 4 semaines par an. #Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;La fourchette de salaire de base prévue pour ce poste dans la région de Montréal est de CAD $88,000 - CAD $110,000. Les échelles salariales dépendent de divers facteurs, notamment les qualifications, l&#39;expérience et la situation géographique. L&#39;échelle n&#39;inclut pas les offres d&#39;actions, les primes ou les avantages potentiels. Votre recruteur peut vous fournir plus d&#39;informations sur l&#39;échelle salariale propre à votre lieu de travail et sur d&#39;autres facteurs au cours du processus d&#39;embauche.&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":4002309002,"name":"People","child_ids":[4063223002,4082048002,4081666002,4004971002,4081662002,4081665002,4081667002,4037818002,4053259002,4081663002,4037813002,4081664002,4037814002,4029398002,4037812002,4038293002,4037816002,4037811002],"parent_id":null}],"offices":[{"id":4038242002,"name":"Montreal Office","location":"Montreal, Canada, Montreal","child_ids":[],"parent_id":4038337002}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":null,"ai_opt_out_request_url":null},{"absolute_url":"https://app.careerpuck.com/job-board/lyft/job/8872142002?gh_jid=8872142002","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"education":"education_optional","employment":"employment_required","internal_job_id":6552537002,"location":{"name":"Montreal, Canada"},"metadata":[{"id":4345907002,"name":"Career Site Category","value":"People","value_type":"single_select"}],"id":8872142002,"updated_at":"2026-10-19T18:43:36-04:00","requisition_id":"111245","title":"People Business Partner, Lyft Urban Solutions","company_name":"Lyft","first_published":"2026-10-06T16:44:23-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;At Lyft, our purpose is to serve and connect. We aim to achieve this by cultivating a work environment where all team members belong and have the opportunity to thrive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lyft Urban Solutions (LUS) creates bikeshare programs that riders love, cities need, and operators value. We design, build and support the bikes and stations technology behind bikeshare programs in cities around the world, including Bixi. Our Montreal team sits at the heart of that work, bringing together engineering, manufacturing, supply chain, operations, marketing and commercial teams under one roof.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the &lt;strong&gt;People Business Partner &lt;/strong&gt;for LUS, you&#39;ll be the go-to people partner, and will also serve as the primary People lead for the Montreal site. You&#39;ll translate business priorities into practical people plans, help managers lead through complex people issues, and make sure our programs land properly in a Quebec context. You&#39;ll report into the Senior People Business Partner for our Global Growth team, and work closely with Employee Relations, Total Rewards, Talent Acquisition, People Operations and Legal.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on role for someone who enjoys being close to the business. Success looks like a deep understanding of the team’s objectives, metrics, performance, and opportunities in order to craft People strategies that enable those objectives. You are equally comfortable coaching a new manager through a difficult conversation and helping a director think through how their team should be structured next year.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partnering with managers and leaders across LUS on team health, performance, development and retention, providing thought partnership that&#39;s direct, practical and grounded in the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading the People responsibilities for the Montreal site, including liaising with CNESST, the OQLF, and running the 1% Training Law program.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage people rhythms autonomously and with excellence: bringing performance reviews, compensation cycles, talent reviews, workforce planning, organizational health reporting and engagement surveys to life for your client groups, and making sure managers are ready for each.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting employee relations matters with care and sound judgement, from first conversation through to resolution, partnering with Employee Relations and Legal where cases are complex.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting organizational changes, from small team restructures to larger shifts in how LUS is organized, including planning, manager preparation, project management and team member communication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Applying Quebec employment law and practice to Lyft&#39;s global programs, and flagging early where something needs to be adapted locally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Using data to spot patterns, such as attrition, engagement and hiring trends, and bringing them to leaders with a clear view on what to do next.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partnering with Finance to track headcount cost, holding leaders accountable and advising on headcount shifts to remain neutral to budget while optimizing for business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Being a visible, trusted presence on site, particularly for teams who don&#39;t sit at a desk all day.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of HR experience, including at least 2–3 years in an HR business partner or generalist role supporting managers directly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of Quebec employment law and experience applying it in practice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional fluency in French and English, written and spoken.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid experience handling employee relations matters, including investigations, performance management and exits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting both salaried, corporate employees and hourly, frontline and / or site-based populations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a company going through integration, restructuring or significant growth preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with HR systems (Workday or similar) and using data to support recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extended health and dental coverage options, along with life insurance and disability benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family building benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pet benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to a Lyft funded Health Care Savings Account&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;RRSP plan with company match to help save for your future&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In addition to provincial observed holidays, salaried team members are covered under Lyft&#39;s flexible paid time off policy. The policy allows team members to take off as much time as they need (with manager approval). Hourly team members get 15 days paid time off, with an additional day for each year of service&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lyft is proud to support new parents with 18 weeks of paid time off, designed as a top-up plan to complement provincial programs. Biological, adoptive, and foster parents are all eligible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subsidized commuter benefits and Lyft ride credits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lyft is committed to creating an inclusive workforce that fosters belonging. Lyft believes that every person has a right to equal employment opportunities without discrimination because of race, ancestry, place of origin, colour, ethnic origin, citizenship, creed, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, marital status, family status, disability, pardoned record of offences, or any other basis protected by applicable law or by Company policy. Lyft also strives for a healthy and safe workplace and strictly prohibits harassment of any kind.&amp;nbsp; Accommodation for persons with disabilities will be provided upon request in accordance with applicable law during the application and hiring process. Please contact your recruiter if you wish to make such a request.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lyft highly values having employees working in-office to foster a collaborative work environment and company culture. This role will be in-office on a hybrid schedule — Team Members will be expected to work in the office at least 3 days per week, including on Mondays, Wednesdays, and Thursdays. Lyft considers working in the office at least 3 days per week to be an essential function of this hybrid role. Your recruiter can share more information about the various in-office perks Lyft offers. Additionally, hybrid roles have the flexibility to work from anywhere for up to 4 weeks per year. #Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The expected base pay range for this position in the Montreal area is CAD $88,000 - CAD $110,000, not inclusive of potential equity offering, bonus or benefits. Salary ranges are dependent on a variety of factors, including qualifications, experience and geographic location. Your recruiter can share more information about the salary range specific to your working location and other factors during the hiring process.&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":4002309002,"name":"People","child_ids":[4063223002,4082048002,4081666002,4004971002,4081662002,4081665002,4081667002,4037818002,4053259002,4081663002,4037813002,4081664002,4037814002,4029398002,4037812002,4038293002,4037816002,4037811002],"parent_id":null}],"offices":[{"id":4038242002,"name":"Montreal Office","location":"Montreal, Canada, Montreal","child_ids":[],"parent_id":4038337002}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":null,"ai_opt_out_request_url":null},{"absolute_url":"https://app.careerpuck.com/job-board/lyft/job/8817974002?gh_jid=8817974002","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"employment":"employment_optional","internal_job_id":6529060002,"location":{"name":"San Francisco, CA"},"metadata":[{"id":4345907002,"name":"Career Site Category","value":"University","value_type":"single_select"}],"id":8817974002,"updated_at":"2026-10-19T18:43:36-04:00","requisition_id":"111200","title":"PhD Machine Learning Software Engineer Intern (Summer 2027)","company_name":"Lyft","first_published":"2026-10-06T16:01:21-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;At Lyft, our purpose is to serve and connect. We aim to achieve this by cultivating a work environment where all team members belong and have the opportunity to thrive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With over half a billion rides and counting, Lyft is solving hard problems in a flourishing domain with a lot of data and creative solutions in Marketplace, Mapping, Fraud, Growth and beyond. We&#39;re actively building the next-generation Machine Learning (ML) platform for low-cost, ultra-immersive transportation to improve people’s lives using modern ML with petabyte-scale data. Our Machine Learning Engineers are excited to work on these challenging problems and redefine solutions to directly impact various aspects of Lyft&#39;s primary business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a PhD Machine Learning Engineer Intern on our Applied AI team, you&#39;ll take on an open research problem tied to product experiences used by millions of riders. Working closely with a Staff ML Engineer mentor, you&#39;ll scope the problem, develop and evaluate new methods on real data, and take the work far enough that it can be shared with the research community, with the goal of a paper submission to a top ML venue.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are a PhD student who enjoys turning open-ended research questions into working systems, and you want your research to be tested against real users and real data, this opportunity is for you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a research project from start to finish: frame the problem, review related work, propose new methods, and design rigorous offline and online evaluations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, train and test ML models in areas such as reinforcement learning, sequential decision-making, personalization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write production-quality code that turns research prototypes into working pipelines on Lyft&#39;s data and ML infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product Managers, Data Scientists, and fellow ML Engineers to frame research questions within the business context&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze experimental and observational data, and communicate findings clearly to both technical and non-technical audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write up results for publication at a peer-reviewed venue, with support from your mentor and the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in code and spec reviews to ensure code quality and distribute knowledge&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Currently pursuing a &lt;strong&gt;PhD &lt;/strong&gt;in Computer Science, Machine Learning, Statistics, Operations Research, Applied Mathematics, or a related technical field, and returning to your program after the internship, with a &lt;strong&gt;graduation date between December 2027 and Summer 2028 (required)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of ML research, shown through publications, preprints, or substantial research projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong foundation in reinforcement learning and sequential decision making, especially problems with delayed or long-horizon rewards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid grounding in both causal inference and counterfactual evaluation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good understanding of ML libraries like PyTorch, TensorFlow, or JAX&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong programming skills in Python or a similar language&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to effectively turn research ML papers into working code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity and ability to quickly learn new concepts and technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem solving mindset, resourcefulness, and willingness to figure things out independently through research or collaboratively through brainstorming&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated oral and written communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Publications at venues such as NeurIPS, ICML, ICLR, KDD, WWW, RecSys, or AAAI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with offline reinforcement learning, off-policy evaluation, or learning from logged interaction data, recommender systems or personalization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical knowledge of how to build efficient end-to-end ML workflows on large-scale data (for example Spark or SQL)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with online experimentation and A/B testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Great medical, dental, and vision insurance options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In addition to holidays, interns receive 2 days paid time off and 3 days sick time off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) plan to help save for your future&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subsidized commuter benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lyft Pink - Lyft team members get an exclusive opportunity to test new benefits of our Ridership Program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Lyft is an equal opportunity employer committed to an inclusive workplace that fosters belonging. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regards to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, age, genetic information, or any other basis prohibited by law. We also consider qualified applicants with criminal histories consistent with applicable federal, state and local law.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Lyft highly values having employees working in-office to foster a collaborative work environment and company culture. This role will be in-office on a hybrid schedule — Team Members will be expected to work in the office 3 days per week on Mondays, Wednesdays, and Thursdays. Lyft considers working in the office at least 3 days per week to be an essential function of this hybrid role. Your recruiter can share more information about the various in-office perks Lyft offers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
