&lt;p&gt;The expected base pay range for this position in the New York City area is $108,000 - $135,000, not inclusive of potential equity offering, bonus or benefits. Salary ranges are dependent on a variety of factors, including qualifications, experience and geographic location. Your recruiter can share more information about the salary range specific to your working location and other factors during the hiring process.&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":4135535002,"name":"Safety Policy","child_ids":[],"parent_id":4094102002}],"offices":[{"id":4000997002,"name":"New York Office","location":"New York, New York, United States","child_ids":[],"parent_id":4032338002},{"id":4000998002,"name":"San Francisco Office","location":"San Francisco, California, United States","child_ids":[],"parent_id":4031979002}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":null,"ai_opt_out_request_url":null},{"absolute_url":"https://app.careerpuck.com/job-board/lyft/job/8888739002?gh_jid=8888739002","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"education":"education_optional","employment":"employment_required","internal_job_id":6559885002,"location":{"name":"Sacramento, CA"},"metadata":[{"id":4345907002,"name":"Career Site Category","value":"Public Policy","value_type":"single_select"}],"id":8888739002,"updated_at":"2026-10-19T18:43:36-04:00","requisition_id":"111258","title":"Public Policy Manager, State & Local (CA)","company_name":"Lyft","first_published":"2026-10-15T16:35:51-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;At Lyft, our purpose is to serve and connect. We aim to achieve this by cultivating a work environment where all team members belong and have the opportunity to thrive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lyft is looking for an experienced Public Policy Manager to join our Policy Team! Based remotely in Sacramento, this position will manage state-level policy efforts in California, as well as Sacramento at the local level. This policy expert will actively work directly with elected officials, policymakers, and key stakeholders. They will engage with a broad range of regulatory and legislative issues critical to the company, ensuring Lyft’s business needs align with evolving policy landscapes. Come join the exciting ride!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute Lyft’s legislative, regulatory, and political strategy at the state level and provide support at the local level mainly in Sacramento (SMF)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, cultivate and manage relationships with strategic third party and business groups, nonprofits and community organizations leveraging Lyft’s internal programs and product offerings, in key markets. Regularly travel to attend community and industry events as needed.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with business, communications and marketing teams to highlight relevant Lyft partnerships, capture key moments, strategize Lyft’s engagement with large events and leverage relationships for business opportunities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Lyft in interactions with elected officials, government agencies, staff, and business groups, including drafting and providing testimony in legislative and regulatory hearings and regularly traveling to attend political events and fundraisers as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track legislation relevant to Lyft and inform company stakeholders and lines of business on legislative and regulatory developments.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop strategic public engagement plans positioning Lyft as a “Force for Good” and reliable thought partner to state officials and third party groups in key markets, while identifying other markets where Lyft’s public engagement could advance Lyft’s legislative and political strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee statewide budget and work cross-functionally with Lyft senior management on developing public policy priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mobilize supporters and activists to show their support during key legislative moments and/or ballot measures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Lyft’s Legal, Compliance, Communications, Campaigns, Social Impact, and Operations teams to align market strategies with regulatory and legislative developments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish deep expertise on Lyft’s public policy priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage external consultants to assist with key Lyft policy priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft comments, talking points, and memos for senior Lyft executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and respond to business groups and government inquiries and requests on policy issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Experience:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5-8 years of political and/or government affairs experience in California.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience directly lobbying elected officials and/or government officials on complex public policy issues in California.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of state-level, county, and municipal policymaking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional strategic and problem-solving skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to thrive in a fast-paced and demanding environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven self-starter with experience leading and winning on complex policy issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Natural connector and relationship builder&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills (written, verbal, and presentation) – you know how to tell a good story and advocate your position&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep relationships with state and local policymakers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing and collaborating with external consultants and lobbyists&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of municipal and state policymaking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of transportation, mobility, technology, autonomous vehicle, gig economy, and future of work policy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience planning and executing stakeholder-facing events, including community engagement initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience directly negotiating,&amp;nbsp; developing relationships and interacting with organized labor is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lyft user / believer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Great medical, dental, and vision insurance options with additional programs available when enrolled&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family building benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Child care and pet benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) plan with company match to help save for your future&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In addition to 12 observed holidays, salaried team members have discretionary paid time off, hourly team members have 15 days paid time off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;18 weeks of paid parental leave. Biological, adoptive, and foster parents are all eligible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subsidized commuter benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly Lyft credits and complimentary Lyft Pink membership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lyft is an equal opportunity employer committed to an inclusive workplace that fosters belonging. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regards to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, age, genetic information, or any other basis prohibited by law. We also consider qualified applicants with criminal histories consistent with applicable federal, state and local law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is fully remote in Sacramento, CA, candidates for this role must be based in the Sacramento metro area. #Remote&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The expected base pay range for this position in the Sacramento area is $131,560 - $164,450, not inclusive of potential equity offering, bonus or benefits. Salary ranges are dependent on a variety of factors, including qualifications, experience and geographic location. Your recruiter can share more information about the salary range specific to your working location and other factors during the hiring process.&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":4140207002,"name":"Western and Southern US Policy","child_ids":[],"parent_id":4002295002}],"offices":[{"id":4038272002,"name":"Flex - CA","location":"California, United States","child_ids":[],"parent_id":4031979002}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":null,"ai_opt_out_request_url":null},{"absolute_url":"https://app.careerpuck.com/job-board/lyft/job/8599054002?gh_jid=8599054002","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"education":"education_optional","employment":"employment_required","internal_job_id":6434400002,"location":{"name":"Nashville, TN"},"metadata":[{"id":4345907002,"name":"Career Site Category","value":"Operations","value_type":"single_select"}],"id":8599054002,"updated_at":"2026-10-19T18:43:36-04:00","requisition_id":"110907","title":"Repair Coordinator ","company_name":"Lyft","first_published":"2026-08-03T11:44:45-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Flexdrive&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Flexdrive, we&#39;re at the forefront of revolutionizing transportation by building the operational backbone for autonomous vehicle (AV) fleets. As a leader in fleet management, we&#39;re leveraging our expertise to enter the AV space, forming strategic partnerships with cutting-edge technology providers. We&#39;re looking for dedicated team members to help us pioneer this new chapter, starting with our first AV depot in Nashville, Tennessee.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Service Lead, Flexdrive is seeking a decisive and security-conscious Repair Coordinator to own the complete repair and parts lifecycle for our 24/7 AV operations — from the initial intake of a vehicle requiring service, through parts procurement and consumption, to the vehicle&#39;s final release back into the active fleet. This role is the central hub for service workflow, technician support, and inventory infrastructure: coordinating work assignments, comprehensive vehicle information, and correct parts availability to minimize vehicle downtime and uphold the high availability standards required for an autonomous fleet. The Repair Coordinator directly impacts the operational efficiency, inventory accuracy, and reliability of Flexdrive&#39;s AV deployment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position offers unique exposure to cutting-edge AV technology and supply chain management in a highly regulated environment. The role requires someone who can balance operational efficiency with uncompromising security standards, provide 24/7 support coverage, and maintain perfect inventory accuracy. If you excel at detailed inventory management, shop-flow coordination, and thrive in mission-critical operations, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Schedule &amp;amp; Shift Availability&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Day Window Shift Pattern&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role supports 24/7 AV depot operations and requires availability to work day window shifts, with hours scheduled between 6:30am - 9:30pm. Specific shift times and schedules will be determined based on operational needs and business requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1. Work Order &amp;amp; Repair Cycle Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Repair Order Processing: &lt;/strong&gt;Initiate work orders from diagnostics, inspections, and automated alerts; assign work to technicians based on skill, workload, and depot priorities; close completed repairs after verifying labor, parts, and &quot;Three Cs&quot; (Complaint, Cause, Correction) documentation in the fleet management system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cycle Time &amp;amp; Labor Oversight: &lt;/strong&gt;Track vehicle downtime against SLAs, escalate stalled repairs (parts delays, diagnostic challenges), and review technician time against standard repair times to flag training needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technician Liaison: &lt;/strong&gt;Communicate repair priorities, parts availability, and work order status between operations and maintenance teams to optimize vehicle turnaround.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2. Inventory &amp;amp; Parts Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Inventory Control &amp;amp; Transactions: &lt;/strong&gt;Manage on-site inventory of AV components, consumables, and spare parts; execute all receipts, consumption, cycle counts, and discrepancy reconciliation through partner inventory systems (SAP), maintaining 99%+ accuracy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Procurement, Kitting &amp;amp; Logistics: &lt;/strong&gt;Track parts deliveries and expedite critical orders to prevent downtime, pre-kit parts for scheduled work orders, and manage inbound freight intake at the dock.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Service-Parts Integration: &lt;/strong&gt;Allocate parts to active work orders and ensure consumption is accurately tracked to the correct vehicle/work order for billing and warranty.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3. Security &amp;amp; Quality Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proprietary Component Security: &lt;/strong&gt;Maintain strict chain-of-custody and secure, limited-access storage for AV proprietary hardware and other high-value components, preventing unauthorized access or disposal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quality &amp;amp; Discrepancy Management: &lt;/strong&gt;Maintain quarantine areas for non-conforming parts, verify inbound shipments against documentation, and report discrepancies (overages, shortages, damage) within 24 hours.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Documentation &amp;amp; SOP Adherence: &lt;/strong&gt;Maintain audit-ready Repair Order and inventory records and conform to all partner service, inventory, and hardware transaction SOPs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4. System Operations &amp;amp; Reporting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fleet &amp;amp; Inventory Systems: &lt;/strong&gt;Log all parts consumption and serial-number tracking in the fleet management system for full lifecycle traceability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reporting &amp;amp; Analytics: &lt;/strong&gt;Generate inventory and service reports, analyzing consumption and cycle-time trends to optimize stock levels, throughput, and carrying costs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5. 24/7 Coordination &amp;amp; Safety&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Shift Continuity: &lt;/strong&gt;Lead daily pass-down meetings and maintain handover documentation covering WIP, down vehicles, and safety campaigns to ensure continuity across shifts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;On-Call &amp;amp; Multi-Site Support: &lt;/strong&gt;Provide on-call mobile support for off-hours crews, travel between depot/warehouse/third-party sites as needed, and coordinate with parts suppliers and repair vendors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Safety &amp;amp; Environmental Compliance: &lt;/strong&gt;Handle hazardous materials and waste streams per EHS/NFPA standards, use required PPE, and safely operate forklifts and pallet jacks per material handling and pedestrian safety protocols.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with ERP or similar inventory management systems (SAP strongly preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to use fleet/shop management tools for work order processing and parts consumption tracking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competency with mobile devices and inventory scanning equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic Microsoft Office/Google Workspace skills for reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of inventory management best practices (FIFO, cycle counting, ABC analysis)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High school diploma or equivalent required; Associate degree in Supply Chain, Logistics, Business, or related field preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience with Shop Management Systems (SMS) or Fleet Management Systems and with ERP systems (SAP strongly preferred), including creating estimates, managing WIP (Work in Progress), inventory transactions, cycle counting, and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience managing high-value or sensitive inventory with strict security requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail with a proven track record of maintaining high fleet availability and inventory accuracy (98%+) while meeting Repair Cycle Time SLAs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with automotive parts nomenclature, identification, and handling procedures preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Physical capabilities including the ability to lift up to 50 lbs unassisted, maneuver heavy automotive components (100+ lbs) using pallet jacks, team lifts, or other material handling equipment, stand/walk for extended periods, and operate material handling equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Forklift Certification: &lt;/strong&gt;Willingness to obtain and maintain OSHA-compliant forklift certification (sit-down/stand-up) within 30 days of hire. Current valid forklift certification and prior heavy-part handling experience is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Valid driver&#39;s license with clean driving record for travel between locations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexibility to work various shifts and provide on-call support during nights/weekends as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Great medical, dental, and vision insurance options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family building benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Salaried team members have unlimited paid time off, hourly team members have 15 days paid time off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) plan to help save for your future&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;18 weeks of paid parental leave. Biological, adoptive, and foster parents are all eligible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pre-tax commuter benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lyft Pink - Lyft team members get an exclusive opportunity to test new benefits of our Ridership Program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;: For this role, candidates must reside in states registered for Flexdrive Services LLC.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is on-site at a Lyft Flexdrive hub or office location full time. #Onsite&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The expected base pay range for this position in the Nashville area is $20.11 - $25.13, not inclusive of potential equity offering, bonus or benefits. Salary ranges are dependent on a variety of factors, including qualifications, experience and geographic location. Your recruiter can share more information about the salary range specific to your working location and other factors during the hiring process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Flexdrive is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to an inclusive workplace that fosters belonging. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regards to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, age, genetic information, or any other basis prohibited by law. Flexdrive also strives for a healthy and safe workplace and strictly prohibits harassment of any kind. Flexdrive will also consider employment for qualified applicants with criminal histories consistent with applicable federal, state and local law.&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":4135513002,"name":"AV & Fleet Operations","child_ids":[],"parent_id":4135512002}],"offices":[{"id":4118460002,"name":"Nashville AV Depot","location":"Nashville, Tennessee, Nashville","child_ids":[],"parent_id":4038194002}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":null,"ai_opt_out_request_url":null},{"absolute_url":"https://app.careerpuck.com/job-board/lyft/job/8840187002?gh_jid=8840187002","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"education":"education_optional","employment":"employment_required","internal_job_id":6538999002,"location":{"name":"Nashville, TN"},"metadata":[{"id":4345907002,"name":"Career Site Category","value":"Operations","value_type":"single_select"}],"id":8840187002,"updated_at":"2026-10-19T18:43:36-04:00","requisition_id":"111212","title":"Repair Operations Lead","company_name":"Lyft","first_published":"2026-09-25T09:51:25-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;At Lyft, our purpose is to serve and connect. We aim to achieve this by cultivating a work environment where all team members belong and have the opportunity to thrive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Flexdrive is a subsidiary of Lyft that works together with Lyft teams to realize our shared mission.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Flexdrive builds the operational backbone for the future of mobility. As a leader in fleet management and a Lyft subsidiary, we&#39;re extending our expertise into autonomous vehicle (AV) infrastructure — managing the physical operations that keep AV fleets safe, available, and performing at scale. Our Nashville depot is the first proof point in a multi-market expansion, and we&#39;re building the team to sustain and scale it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the &lt;strong&gt;Operations Manager, AV Deployment,&lt;/strong&gt; Flexdrive is seeking an exceptional Repair Operations Lead to help run the day-to-day service operations supporting our AV fleet. You&#39;ll work alongside a second Repair Operations Lead as a partnered pair, sharing coverage and accountability for the floor. This is a people-first leadership role. You will lead and mentor our repair coordinators, hold both the coordinator team and our on-site technicians (a 3rd party partner) accountable to quality and turnaround expectations, and keep the partnership running smoothly so the fleet stays available.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a strong people leader rather than a deep technical expert. Service advisor or service drive experience is helpful because you&#39;ll be fluent in the workflow, but what matters most is your ability to develop a team, set clear expectations, and hold the line on them without losing the room. You should be comfortable managing an external partner relationship day to day, balancing a collaborative working rapport with firm accountability. You bring a teamwork mentality, genuinely care about employee relations and the culture you&#39;re building, and will lean into Lyft&#39;s values as one of the early leaders shaping how this site operates. If you&#39;re energized by growing people, building strong partner relationships, and bringing order to a fast-moving operation, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shift Pattern&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This role supports 24/7 AV depot operations and requires availability to work day shifts, with hours scheduled between 5:00 PM - 1:30 AM, with alternating weekends with rotating weekdays off.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Specific shift times and schedules will be determined based on operational needs and business requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Schedules will include weekends and holidays based on depot operational requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Team Management&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partnership Oversight &amp;amp; Accountability: Serve as the day-to-day point of accountability for our onsite repair partner, holding their technicians to agreed quality, turnaround, and certification standards across all shifts, and escalating gaps through the right channels before they affect fleet availability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workflow Distribution: Manage and optimize repair workflows across technician teams, balancing workload, prioritizing critical repairs, and ensuring SLA compliance for all maintenance activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-Functional Partnership: Work closely with the internal teams that own our third-party relationships and offsite collision repairs, acting as the site-level point of contact so vehicles route correctly, status stays visible, and repair timelines hold. You&#39;ll surface issues from the floor to those teams and carry their requirements back to the site so both sides stay aligned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performance Management: Conduct regular performance reviews, skills assessments, and development planning for technical staff, fostering a culture of safety, continuous improvement and technical excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Development &amp;amp; Coaching&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Onboarding &amp;amp; Job Task Training: Get new repair coordinators up to speed on their core responsibilities — work order management, vehicle intake and staging, documentation, and the systems they&#39;ll live in day to day — so they&#39;re contributing confidently and correctly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Depot Operations Fluency: Teach the team how the depot actually runs: how work flows from intake through repair and release, how their role connects to the technicians and the internal teams upstream and downstream, and what good looks like at each handoff.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ongoing Coaching &amp;amp; Mentorship: Provide regular, direct feedback through side-by-sides, one-on-ones, and in-the-moment coaching. Identify where each coordinator wants to grow, build a path for them, and address performance gaps early and honestly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fleet Health &amp;amp; Maintenance Operations&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fleet Performance Optimization: Monitor and improve key metrics including Mean Time to Recovery, Vehicle Turnaround Time, and Diagnosis Escalation Rate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Service Quality Assurance: Implement and maintain quality control processes ensuring all maintenance work meets partner specifications and safety standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintenance Planning: Develop and execute preventive maintenance schedules, manage maintenance change requests, and ensure compliance with partner fleet management system requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical Problem Resolution: Lead root cause analysis for technical issues working with our 3rd party partner, implementing corrective actions, and developing preventive measures to reduce repeat failures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Parts &amp;amp; Materials Oversight&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Service and Parts Coordinator Management: Directly supervise parts and service writing coordination, ensuring seamless integration between parts allocation, work order documentation, and inventory management while maintaining accuracy and compliance standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supply Chain Coordination: Oversee Material Coordinator activities, ensuring optimal parts inventory levels, secure storage of proprietary components, and compliance with chain of custody standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inventory Optimization: Analyze parts consumption patterns, forecast requirements, and coordinate with partner aftermarket teams to prevent stockouts while minimizing carrying costs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vendor Parts Management: Manage relationships with parts suppliers, negotiate service agreements, and ensure timely delivery of critical components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Non-Conforming Parts Process: Oversee quarantine and disposition procedures for non-conforming parts, ensuring proper documentation and handling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance &amp;amp; Documentation&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Training Compliance: Ensure all personnel maintain required qualifications through partner learning management systems, conducting monthly verification reviews per standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Safety Program Integration: Collaborate with the safety team to ensure all maintenance activities comply with EHS requirements, including battery safety, hazardous materials handling, and hot work procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Documentation Management: Maintain comprehensive documentation hierarchy including job descriptions, safety protocols, training records, and maintenance logs per partner requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regulatory Compliance: Ensure all technical operations meet federal, state, and local regulations including EPA, OSHA, and AV-specific requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Planning &amp;amp; Continuous Improvement&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operational Excellence: Drive continuous improvement initiatives, analyzing performance data to identify optimization opportunities and implement best practices across technical operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capacity Planning: Forecast staffing needs, training requirements, and infrastructure upgrades to support fleet growth and operational scaling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration: Partner with Operations Manager, Depot Operations Leads, and partner technical teams to ensure seamless integration of maintenance and depot operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge Management: Establish and maintain technical knowledge base, documenting lessons learned, best practices, and troubleshooting guides for common issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Culture of Safety:&amp;nbsp; Champion a comprehensive culture of safety through proactive engagement.&amp;nbsp; Leading by example in following all safety requirements; educating the team on safety protocols; proactively identifying risks; managing incidents, including reporting and investigation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Competencies&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced diagnostic skills for electric and autonomous vehicle systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with fleet management systems (Carman experience preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SAP or similar ERP system expertise for parts and maintenance tracking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data analysis and reporting capabilities for performance metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of ISO quality standards and automotive compliance requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Automotive Technology, Mechanical Engineering, Operations Management, or related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of progressive experience in fleet maintenance management, automotive service operations, or technical training leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience managing technical teams including hiring, training, performance management, and development of skilled technicians.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience developing and delivering technical training programs, preferably in automotive or fleet maintenance environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven expertise in electric vehicle systems, diagnostic procedures, and advanced automotive technologies (AV experience highly preferred).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of maintenance management systems, KPI tracking, and data-driven decision making for fleet operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with vendor management, contract negotiation, and third-party service provider oversight.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success implementing quality management systems, safety management systems&amp;nbsp; and continuous improvement methodologies (Six Sigma, Lean preferred).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication skills with ability to interface effectively with technical teams, executive leadership, and external partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Current ASE certifications preferred; ability to obtain required partner certifications within 90 days.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Valid driver&#39;s license with clean driving record.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Great medical, dental, and vision insurance options with additional programs available when enrolled&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family building benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Child care and pet benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) plan with company match to help save for your future&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In addition to 12 observed holidays, salaried team members have discretionary paid time off, hourly team members have 15 days paid time off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;18 weeks of paid parental leave. Biological, adoptive, and foster parents are all eligible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subsidized commuter benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly Lyft credits and complimentary Lyft Pink membership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;: For this role, candidates must reside in states registered for Flexdrive Services LLC.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is on-site at a Lyft Flexdrive hub or office location full time. #Onsite&lt;/p&gt;
