&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Code Quality:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Write production-level code and participate in code reviews to ensure quality and share knowledge across the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;M.S. or Ph.D. in Computer Science or related technical field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years (or Ph.D. with 3+ years) of experience in machine learning modelling or related fields&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with deep learning technologies for recommendation systems, including TensorFlow, PyTorch, or similar frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of statistical concepts such as hypothesis testing, regression analysis, and performance evaluation metrics for machine learning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with translating state-of-the-art ML research into production systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Python, Golang, or other programming language&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to tackle ambiguous problems and deliver solutions at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and interpersonal skills for effective cross-functional collaboration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Great medical, dental, and vision insurance options with additional programs available when enrolled&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family building benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Child care and pet benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) plan with company match to help save for your future&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In addition to 12 observed holidays, salaried team members have discretionary paid time off, hourly team members have 15 days paid time off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;18 weeks of paid parental leave. Biological, adoptive, and foster parents are all eligible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subsidized commuter benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly Lyft credits and complimentary Lyft Pink membership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lyft is an equal opportunity employer committed to an inclusive workplace that fosters belonging. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regards to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, age, genetic information, or any other basis prohibited by law. We also consider qualified applicants with criminal histories consistent with applicable federal, state and local law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lyft highly values having employees working in-office to foster a collaborative work environment and company culture. This role will be in-office on a hybrid schedule — Team Members will be expected to work in the office 3 days per week on Mondays, Wednesdays, and Thursdays. Lyft considers working in the office at least 3 days per week to be an essential function of this hybrid role. Your recruiter can share more information about the various in-office perks Lyft offers. Additionally, hybrid roles have the flexibility to work from anywhere for up to 4 weeks per year. #Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The expected base pay range for this position in the San Francisco area is $162,800 - $203,500, not inclusive of potential equity offering, bonus or benefits. Salary ranges are dependent on a variety of factors, including qualifications, experience and geographic location. Your recruiter can share more information about the salary range specific to your working location and other factors during the hiring process.&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":4094258002,"name":"Core Rider","child_ids":[],"parent_id":4082089002}],"offices":[{"id":4000998002,"name":"San Francisco Office","location":"San Francisco, California, United States","child_ids":[],"parent_id":4031979002}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":null,"ai_opt_out_request_url":null},{"absolute_url":"https://app.careerpuck.com/job-board/lyft/job/8908002002?gh_jid=8908002002","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"education":"education_optional","employment":"employment_required","internal_job_id":6568656002,"location":{"name":"Toronto, Canada"},"metadata":[{"id":4345907002,"name":"Career Site Category","value":"Data Analytics & Business Intelligence","value_type":"single_select"}],"id":8908002002,"updated_at":"2026-10-22T11:40:11-04:00","requisition_id":"111289","title":"Senior Manager, Global Workforce Planning","company_name":"Lyft","first_published":"2026-10-22T11:40:11-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;At Lyft, our purpose is to serve and connect. We aim to achieve this by cultivating a work environment where all team members belong and have the opportunity to thrive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lyft&#39;s Customer Care Operations team handles more than 1.7 million customer interactions every month. We support riders, drivers, and businesses across voice, chat, and messaging, through in-house teams and a global network of outsourced partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Senior Manager, Global Workforce &amp;amp; Partner Management, you&#39;ll own how our global workforce is sized, scheduled, funded, and protected. You&#39;ll turn demand into capacity, manage the spend behind it, and own the business relationship with our outsourced partners. You&#39;ll work hand in hand with the Support Operations leaders who own service delivery and quality, giving them the plans, insights, and partner capacity they need to deliver for customers. Reporting to the Director, Global Strategy &amp;amp; Operations, you&#39;ll lead Forecasting, Financial Planning &amp;amp; Management, and Workforce Management, including Scheduling &amp;amp; Real-Time Operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Plan the workforce. &lt;/strong&gt;Own short- and long-range forecasting and capacity planning across channels, queues, languages, and lines of business. Lock and deliver rolling billable hour forecasts to our partners, so they can staff accurately and we can hold them accountable to the plan. Build the models behind our annual and half-year plans, and stress-test them as the business and AI adoption evolve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hold teams accountable to the plan. &lt;/strong&gt;Make sure in-house and partner teams staff to the forecast, schedule to requirements, and keep agents adherent and productive. Own forecast accuracy, staffing to plan, schedule adherence, occupancy, and shrinkage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manage the queues. &lt;/strong&gt;Monitor handle time, resolution time, and wait times in real time. When wait times degrade or a mass defect hits, lead urgent queue management to protect customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Give leadership clear visibility.&lt;/strong&gt; Set the goals, scorecards, and business reviews that show how we&#39;re performing on staffing, cost, and partner health. Develop and communicate concise, evidence-based narratives for leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own workforce spend.&lt;/strong&gt; Manage the Customer Care workforce budget with Finance across both internal and outsourced agents. Track cost per contact and the drivers behind it, such as headcount, overtime, and utilization. Govern partner billing end to end, including billable hours, rate structures, invoice accuracy, and performance-based credits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the partner business relationship.&lt;/strong&gt; Manage the commercial side of our BPO partnerships, including contracts, governance cadences, executive business reviews, and commercial escalations. Partner with Procurement on new agreements and renewals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be a trusted partner to Support Operations.&lt;/strong&gt; Work alongside the support operations leaders who own service delivery and quality, so their customer goals and KPIs are met. Surface the insights that move productivity, wait times, and customer experience, and turn them into action together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape our footprint and resilience.&lt;/strong&gt; Influence where work is done and by whom, including vendor allocation, site strategy, and location mix. Plan and test business continuity so capacity can shift quickly when disruptions hit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;See around corners.&lt;/strong&gt; Serve as Customer Care&#39;s primary point of contact with Product, Tech, and business leaders on what&#39;s changing across Lyft, from ride volume and AI improvements to launches, global growth, integrations, and new partnerships. Size and scope the support impact early so we&#39;re staffed, funded, and ready from day one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Make the case for investment.&lt;/strong&gt; Size opportunities, articulate trade-offs, and build the business cases that fund strategic priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build a best-in-class function.&lt;/strong&gt; Get the most out of our workforce management tools and tech stack. Automate manual work, improve data and reporting, and make planning faster and more accurate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build the team, inside and out.&lt;/strong&gt; Hire, develop, and lead a team of managers and analysts, with clear ownership across a function where finance, operations, and technology meet. Extend that leadership to the workforce teams at our outsourced partners by setting clear goals for productivity, staffing, and scheduling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years in contact center workforce management, support operations, or operations strategy, including 5+ years leading managers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of owning workforce planning for a large, global, multi-channel, multi-language operation with both in-house and outsourced teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert command of workforce execution metrics, including forecast accuracy, staffing to plan, adherence, occupancy, shrinkage, handle time, and wait time. You know how to hold in-house and partner teams accountable to them and how to stabilize queues quickly when things go wrong.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning the commercial relationship with BPO partners at enterprise scale, including contracts, billing models, footprint, and site decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong financial foundation. You&#39;ve owned a workforce budget across internal and outsourced agents, managed cost per contact, and can turn capacity models into a clear story for Finance and senior leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading through influence, both with support operations leaders whose goals you help deliver and with partner teams you don&#39;t directly manage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience sizing the support impact of growth, launches, integrations, or new partnerships, ideally in a marketplace or platform business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building business continuity plans across multiple vendors and regions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with enterprise WFM tools, plus a builder&#39;s mindset for automating manual work and improving data and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical AI fluency. You understand how automation changes demand, staffing, and partner economics, and you can lead teams through that shift.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re a trusted partner to Finance, Product, Tech, and Operations, and you&#39;re clear, direct, and decisive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extended health and dental coverage options, along with life insurance and disability benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family building benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Child care and pet benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to a Lyft funded Health Care Savings Account&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;RRSP plan to help save for your future&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In addition to provincial observed holidays, salaried team members are covered under Lyft&#39;s flexible paid time off policy. The policy allows team members to take off as much time as they need (with manager approval). Hourly team members get 15 days paid time off, with an additional day for each year of service&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lyft is proud to support new parents with 18 weeks of paid time off, designed as a top-up plan to complement provincial programs. Biological, adoptive, and foster parents are all eligible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subsidized commuter benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Lyft is committed to creating an inclusive workforce that fosters belonging. Lyft believes that every person has a right to equal employment opportunities without discrimination because of race, ancestry, place of origin, colour, ethnic origin, citizenship, creed, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, marital status, family status, disability, pardoned record of offences, or any other basis protected by applicable law or by Company policy. Lyft also strives for a healthy and safe workplace and strictly prohibits harassment of any kind.&amp;nbsp; Accommodation for persons with disabilities will be provided upon request in accordance with applicable law during the application and hiring process. Please contact your recruiter if you wish to make such a request.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Lyft highly values having employees working in-office to foster a collaborative work environment and company culture. This role will be in-office on a hybrid schedule — Team Members will be expected to work in the office at least 3 days per week, including on Mondays, Wednesdays, and Thursdays. Lyft considers working in the office at least 3 days per week to be an essential function of this hybrid role. Your recruiter can share more information about the various in-office perks Lyft offers. Additionally, hybrid roles have the flexibility to work from anywhere for up to 4 weeks per year. #Hybrid&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The expected base pay range for this position in the Toronto area is CAD $194,000 - $242,500, not inclusive of potential equity offering, bonus or benefits. Salary ranges are dependent on a variety of factors, including qualifications, experience and geographic location. Your recruiter can share more information about the salary range specific to your working location and other factors during the hiring process.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Lyft may use artificial intelligence to screen applicants, however, Lyft employees make the ultimate selection and hiring decisions.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This is a new position.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":4135533002,"name":"Core Support Ops","child_ids":[],"parent_id":4094102002}],"offices":[{"id":4139788002,"name":"Toronto Office","location":"Toronto, Canada, Toronto","child_ids":[],"parent_id":4038198002}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":null,"ai_opt_out_request_url":null},{"absolute_url":"https://app.careerpuck.com/job-board/lyft/job/8908000002?gh_jid=8908000002","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"education":"education_optional","employment":"employment_required","internal_job_id":6568655002,"location":{"name":"Nashville, TN"},"metadata":[{"id":4345907002,"name":"Career Site Category","value":"Accounting & Finance","value_type":"single_select"}],"id":8908000002,"updated_at":"2026-10-23T18:19:53-04:00","requisition_id":"111286","title":"Senior Payroll Analyst","company_name":"Lyft","first_published":"2026-10-23T18:19:53-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;At Lyft, our purpose is to serve and connect. We aim to achieve this by cultivating a work environment where all team members belong and have the opportunity to thrive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lyft is looking for a highly motivated individual to join our Accounting team as a Senior Payroll Analyst. This role will assist in the processing of bi-weekly payrolls in the US and Canada, maintaining related records, and developing and documenting various Payroll policies and procedures. &amp;nbsp;This role will also assist in payroll processing and related tax reporting for the Company’s quarterly equity vesting process and ESPP plan, as well as manage the Leave of Absence process for payroll. This candidate must be able to demonstrate the ability to work and thrive in a fast paced, dynamic and rapidly changing environment. This candidate must be a team player who can work independently.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for payroll processing for assigned payrolls, US and/or International&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for processing inputs from compensation and benefits, including&amp;nbsp; auditing benefits, compensation, and leave of absence data for assigned payrolls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate LOA payments and return to work dates with vendor&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with relocation team on relocation data for employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in the audit process of payroll taxes related to the Company’s quarterly equity vesting process, as well as its ESPP plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain SOX compliance in areas of responsibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in the development and documentation of various Payroll initiatives designed to streamline the process and scale with the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and reconcile payroll records&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide prompt, courteous, and efficient customer service to employees who have questions regarding their pay, deductions, paid leave balances and other payroll processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure accurate and timely preparation of required tax reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with HR, Benefits, IT, Finance, and Accounting teams to develop and improve processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare ad hoc reports as needed and perform other duties as assigned&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BS degree in Accounting, Business, Finance or equivalent experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of relevant experience in payroll; experience with mobile workforce, multi-jurisdictional payroll, multiple country processing and equity vesting processes preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be detail-oriented with excellent organization, oral and written communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced computer skills: Microsoft Excel and Word&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior Workday, ADP Globalview and Dayforce experience are highly desirable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Great medical, dental, and vision insurance options with additional programs available when enrolled&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family building benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Child care and pet benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) plan to help save for your future&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In addition to 12 observed holidays, salaried team members have discretionary paid time off, hourly team members have 15 days paid time off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;18 weeks of paid parental leave. Biological, adoptive, and foster parents are all eligible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subsidized commuter benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lyft Pink - Lyft team members get an exclusive opportunity to test new benefits of our Ridership Program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Lyft is an equal opportunity employer committed to an inclusive workplace that fosters belonging. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regards to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, age, genetic information, or any other basis prohibited by law. We also consider qualified applicants with criminal histories consistent with applicable federal, state and local law.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Lyft highly values having employees working in-office to foster a collaborative work environment and company culture. This role will be in-office on a hybrid schedule following the establishment of a Lyft office in Nashville — Team Members will be expected to work in the office 3 days per week on Mondays, Wednesdays, and Thursdays. Lyft considers working in the office at least 3 days per week to be an essential function of this hybrid role. Additionally, hybrid roles have the flexibility to work from anywhere for up to 4 weeks per year. #Hybrid&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The expected base pay range for this position in the Nashville area is $72,160 - $90,200. Salary ranges are dependent on a variety of factors, including qualifications, experience and geographic location. Range is not inclusive of potential equity offering, bonus or benefits. Your recruiter can share more information about the salary range specific to your working location and other factors during the hiring process.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":4002291002,"name":"Finance","child_ids":[4092665002,4135508002,4092664002,4082049002,4082050002,4082052002,4082054002,4082055002,4082056002,4082057002,4094251002,4082053002,4002292002,4030999002,4002293002,4048549002],"parent_id":4042810002}],"offices":[{"id":4038287002,"name":"Flex - TN","location":"Tennessee, United States","child_ids":[],"parent_id":4038194002},{"id":4040669002,"name":"Nashville Union Coworking","location":"Nashville, Tennessee, United States","child_ids":[],"parent_id":4038194002}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":null,"ai_opt_out_request_url":null},{"absolute_url":"https://app.careerpuck.com/job-board/lyft/job/8872290002?gh_jid=8872290002","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"education":"education_optional","employment":"employment_required","internal_job_id":6552602002,"location":{"name":"New York, NY"},"metadata":[{"id":4345907002,"name":"Career Site Category","value":"People","value_type":"single_select"}],"id":8872290002,"updated_at":"2026-10-19T18:43:36-04:00","requisition_id":"111246","title":"Senior PBP, Finance","company_name":"Lyft","first_published":"2026-10-06T18:04:06-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;At Lyft, our purpose is to serve and connect. We aim to achieve this by cultivating a work environment where all team members belong and have the opportunity to thrive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As &lt;strong&gt;Senior People Business Partner&lt;/strong&gt; for Finance, you&#39;ll be the strategic people partner to Finance leadership. Lyft&#39;s Finance organization spans FP&amp;amp;A, accounting, tax, treasury, investor relations, procurement, and increasingly operates across multiple countries and legal entities as Lyft grows internationally. You&#39;ll help shape how the organization is structured, how it plans its workforce, how it builds and keeps its talent, and how it adapts as the business changes. You&#39;ll be a trusted, candid advisor to our CFO and Finance leadership team, someone who understands the numbers as well as the people, and who is confident enough to push back when the plan doesn&#39;t add up.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll report into People Business Partner leadership and work closely with Total Rewards, Talent Acquisition, Employee Relations, Team Member Experience and Legal. This role carries significant scope and autonomy, and suits someone who can operate at executive level while still getting into the details when it matters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advising Finance leadership, up to the executive level, on the people implications of business decisions, bringing a clear point of view rather than a list of options.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading organizational design across Finance: spans and layers, team structures, role clarity and the reorganizations that come with growth, integration and change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owning workforce planning and talent strategy for the Finance organisation: headcount, skills, location strategy and the trade-offs between them; talent reviews, succession planning, leadership development, and retention of critical people, including across newly integrated international teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guiding leaders through complex change, including restructures and M&amp;amp;A integration, with a clear plan, well-prepared managers and honest communication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shaping compensation and performance decisions through the annual cycle, making sure outcomes are fair, well-reasoned and defensible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coaching senior leaders on their leadership, their teams and the conversations they&#39;d rather avoid.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Using people data and insight to show leaders what&#39;s really happening in their organization and what to do about it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handling sensitive and high-risk matters with discretion and judgement, partnering with Employee Relations and Legal as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of progressive HR experience, including substantial time as a senior HR business partner supporting director, VP and executive-level leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of leading organizational design and change at scale, with measurable results you can point to.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to influence senior stakeholders, including when you&#39;re delivering a message they don&#39;t want to hear.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound judgement on complex employee relations and high-risk people matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong business and financial acumen. You&#39;re comfortable in a budget conversation and can hold your own with finance professionals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort using AI tools and people analytics to work faster and make better-informed recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Preferred: Experience supporting Finance or other corporate (G&amp;amp;A) functions, and with multi-country or multi-entity organizations, including international employment considerations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Preferred: Exposure to M&amp;amp;A integration or large-scale restructuring, in tech,&amp;nbsp; or marketplace environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Great medical, dental, and vision insurance options with additional programs available when enrolled&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family building benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Child care and pet benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) plan with company match to help save for your future&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In addition to 12 observed holidays, salaried team members have discretionary paid time off, hourly team members have 15 days paid time off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;18 weeks of paid parental leave. Biological, adoptive, and foster parents are all eligible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subsidized commuter benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly Lyft credits and complimentary Lyft Pink membership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lyft is an equal opportunity employer committed to an inclusive workplace that fosters belonging. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regards to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, age, genetic information, or any other basis prohibited by law. We also consider qualified applicants with criminal histories consistent with applicable federal, state and local law.&lt;/p&gt;
