&lt;p&gt;Lyft is an equal opportunity employer committed to an inclusive workplace that fosters belonging. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regards to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, age, genetic information, or any other basis prohibited by law. We also consider qualified applicants with criminal histories consistent with applicable federal, state and local law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lyft highly values having employees working in-office to foster a collaborative work environment and company culture. This role will be in-office on a hybrid schedule — Team Members will be expected to work in the office 3 days per week on Mondays, Wednesdays, and Thursdays. Lyft considers working in the office at least 3 days per week to be an essential function of this hybrid role. Your recruiter can share more information about the various in-office perks Lyft offers. Additionally, hybrid roles have the flexibility to work from anywhere for up to 4 weeks per year. #Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The expected base pay range for this position in the New York City area is $176,000 - $220,000, not inclusive of potential equity offering, bonus or benefits. Salary ranges are dependent on a variety of factors, including qualifications, experience and geographic location. Your recruiter can share more information about the salary range specific to your working location and other factors during the hiring process.&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":4069022002,"name":"Lyft Ads","child_ids":[],"parent_id":4135522002}],"offices":[{"id":4000997002,"name":"New York Office","location":"New York, New York, United States","child_ids":[],"parent_id":4032338002}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":null,"ai_opt_out_request_url":null},{"absolute_url":"https://app.careerpuck.com/job-board/lyft/job/8639319002?gh_jid=8639319002","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"education":"education_optional","employment":"employment_required","internal_job_id":6450401002,"location":{"name":"Ukraine Anywhere"},"metadata":[{"id":4345907002,"name":"Career Site Category","value":"Software Engineering","value_type":"single_select"}],"id":8639319002,"updated_at":"2026-10-19T18:43:36-04:00","requisition_id":"111003","title":"Staff Software Engineer","company_name":"Lyft","first_published":"2026-07-17T23:19:00-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;At Lyft, our purpose is to serve and connect. We aim to achieve this by cultivating a work environment where all team members belong and have the opportunity to thrive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Global Support &amp;amp; Partnerships team is a critical and unique part of helping Lyft succeed in our purpose to Serve and Connect. We support Lyft&#39;s international growth by developing integration platforms that seamlessly link global customers to an exceptional customer care experience.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We go beyond simply supporting customers; we build the foundational infrastructure that turns every support interaction into a moment of genuine connection. Whether supporting our established North American community or welcoming new users worldwide, we ensure a unified, reliable, and efficient experience for riders, drivers, applicants and support agents alike. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an experienced technical leader who can support our global ambition by designing, owning, and scaling the Global Support Platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the technical vision and strategy for a rapidly evolving product area, making high-judgment calls on architecture and technology direction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the adoption of AI and machine learning solutions to optimize customer support workflows and enhance operational efficiency across the platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead a team of talented engineers who ship code and tackle hard engineering problems, maintaining a high bar for technical excellence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate high-level business goals into actionable engineering projects. Own the technical roadmap from conception to delivery, managing cross-team dependencies and mitigating risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the responsible adoption of AI development tools across engineering teams - modeling effective use, establishing best practices, and mentoring engineers to improve productivity without compromising code quality or security.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion improvements in system, observability, performance, and tech debt reduction, extending your influence beyond your immediate team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish best practices for deployment, alerting, and on-call health. Take holistic ownership of the platform&#39;s stability, tracking down issue root causes and building preventive safeguards for your immediate scope and beyond.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive alignment across product, design, and operations. Proactively resolve bottlenecks and make decisive trade-offs to protect system architecture from competing organizational priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and level up the engineers around you. Delegate stretch opportunities, lead cross-team reviews, and foster a culture of strong technical excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of software engineering industry experience with a track record of architecting and delivering large-scale backend systems in production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience setting technical direction for a product or platform area, including authoring architecture docs and driving alignment across senior stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in designing and operating distributed systems — microservices, event-driven architectures, and high-throughput APIs at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong proficiency in one or more backend languages (Python, Go, Java, C#, or similar) and a solid understanding of performance, concurrency, and reliability tradeoffs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with public cloud platforms (e.g., AWS, GCP, Microsoft Azure) and modern container orchestration technologies (e.g., Kubernetes, Docker, cri-o).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead and influence a team of engineers, including setting technical standards, running design reviews, and unblocking execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills — able to represent the team&#39;s technical strategy clearly to leadership and align cross-functional partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Full-stack versatility: while the role is server-focused, the ability to own frontend development when needed and deliver features end-to-end is a strong plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional and stable working environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The latest technology and equipment you need.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Potential to work remotely, including out of country (dependent on work authorizations).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;28 calendar days for vacation and up to 5 paid sick days.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;18 weeks of paid parental leave. Biological, adoptive and foster parents are all eligible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health benefits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family building benefits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is fully remote in Ukraine, however, employees are required to live and work in Ukraine in order to be qualified for this position. #Remote&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":4135539002,"name":"SCC Tech","child_ids":[],"parent_id":4094102002}],"offices":[{"id":4049039002,"name":"Flex - Ukraine","location":"Kyiv, Kyiv, Ukraine","child_ids":[],"parent_id":4038220002}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":null,"ai_opt_out_request_url":null},{"absolute_url":"https://app.careerpuck.com/job-board/lyft/job/8688631002?gh_jid=8688631002","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"education":"education_optional","employment":"employment_required","internal_job_id":6471357002,"location":{"name":"San Francisco, CA"},"metadata":[{"id":4345907002,"name":"Career Site Category","value":"Software Engineering","value_type":"single_select"}],"id":8688631002,"updated_at":"2026-10-19T18:43:36-04:00","requisition_id":"111063","title":"Staff Software Engineer, Lyft Business","company_name":"Lyft","first_published":"2026-08-10T16:20:03-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;At Lyft, our purpose is to serve and connect. We aim to achieve this by cultivating a work environment where all team members belong and have the opportunity to thrive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Lyft Business organization builds the platform that lets organizations move the people they depend on employees, clients, and customers. From the foundational mechanics of a company funding and provisioning a ride to the tailored workflows that get an employee to a client meeting or home after a late shift, we sweat the small stuff to make Lyft the transportation solution businesses build their programs on.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Staff Software Engineer on the Lyft Business Team, you will act as a critical technical leader, taking holistic ownership of complex systems that span the rider experience, the administrator experience, and the enterprise integrations behind them — defining strategic roadmaps, driving cross-functional alignment, and driving engineering excellence to improve how organizations move their people.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape the long-term architecture for systems, taking accountability for both short-term functionality and long-term health&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate high-level business goals into actionable engineering projects. Own the technical roadmap from conception to delivery, managing cross-team dependencies and mitigating risks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion improvements in system, observability, performance, and tech debt reduction, extending your influence beyond your immediate team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish best practices for deployment, alerting, and on-call health. Take holistic ownership of the platform&#39;s stability, tracking down issues root causes and building preventive safeguards for your immediate scope and beyond.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive alignment across product, design, and operations. Proactively resolve bottlenecks and make decisive trade-offs to protect system architecture from competing organizational priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and level up the engineers around you. Delegate stretch opportunities, lead cross-team reviews, and foster a culture of strong technical excellence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a dependable, high-bar interviewer and active participant in Lyft’s broader internal engineering community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Experience:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BS/MS or equivalent in Computer Engineering, Computer Science, or a related field, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of software engineering industry experience, with a proven track record of technical leadership and system ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in designing, debugging, and running fault-tolerant, highly available, large-scale distributed systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience driving technical roadmaps, managing cross-team dependencies, and influencing system architecture at an organizational level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid knowledge of distributed systems, relational databases, and NoSQL databases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with public cloud platforms (e.g., AWS, GCP, Microsoft Azure) and modern container orchestration technologies (e.g., Kubernetes, Docker, cri-o).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to communicate complex technical trade-offs effectively to both technical and non-technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work with a low-ego, highly collaborative, and cross-functional mindset while actively lifting up the engineers around you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Great medical, dental, and vision insurance options with additional programs available when enrolled&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family building benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Child care and pet benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) plan with company match to help save for your future&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In addition to 12 observed holidays, salaried team members have discretionary paid time off, hourly team members have 15 days paid time off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;18 weeks of paid parental leave. Biological, adoptive, and foster parents are all eligible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subsidized commuter benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly Lyft credits and complimentary Lyft Pink membership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lyft is an equal opportunity employer committed to an inclusive workplace that fosters belonging. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regards to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, age, genetic information, or any other basis prohibited by law. We also consider qualified applicants with criminal histories consistent with applicable federal, state and local law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lyft highly values having employees working in-office to foster a collaborative work environment and company culture. This role will be in-office on a hybrid schedule — Team Members will be expected to work in the office 3 days per week on Mondays, Wednesdays, and Thursdays. Lyft considers working in the office at least 3 days per week to be an essential function of this hybrid role. Your recruiter can share more information about the various in-office perks Lyft offers. Additionally, hybrid roles have the flexibility to work from anywhere for up to 4 weeks per year. #Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The expected base pay range for this position in the San Francisco area is $176,000 - $220,000, not inclusive of potential equity offering, bonus or benefits. Salary ranges are dependent on a variety of factors, including qualifications, experience and geographic location. Your recruiter can share more information about the salary range specific to your working location and other factors during the hiring process.&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":4092657002,"name":"Lyft Business","child_ids":[],"parent_id":4135522002}],"offices":[{"id":4000998002,"name":"San Francisco Office","location":"San Francisco, California, United States","child_ids":[],"parent_id":4031979002}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":null,"ai_opt_out_request_url":null},{"absolute_url":"https://app.careerpuck.com/job-board/lyft/job/8862007002?gh_jid=8862007002","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"employment":"employment_optional","internal_job_id":6547818002,"location":{"name":"Longueuil, Canada"},"metadata":[{"id":4345907002,"name":"Career Site Category","value":"University","value_type":"single_select"}],"id":8862007002,"updated_at":"2026-10-19T18:43:36-04:00","requisition_id":"111236","title":"Stagiaire en ingénierie de la qualité terrain, matériel (été 2027)","company_name":"Lyft","first_published":"2026-10-02T15:58:29-04:00","language":"fr","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;Chez Lyft, notre raison d&#39;être est de servir et de connecter. Lyft Urban Solutions conçoit, fabrique et exploite des systèmes de vélopartage dans plus de 50 villes à travers le monde, dont New York, Chicago, Londres, Barcelone, Mexico, Rio de Janeiro et Montréal. Notre usine de Longueuil est le berceau de BIXI, le premier système de vélopartage automatisé en Amérique du Nord, et fabrique aujourd&#39;hui les vélos et les stations de certains des plus grands réseaux de vélopartage au monde.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nous recherchons un ou une &lt;strong&gt;stagiaire en ingénierie de la qualité terrain, matériel&lt;/strong&gt; pour se joindre à notre équipe Qualité terrain (Field Quality) à notre établissement de Longueuil. Une fois que nos vélos, vélos électriques, batteries et stations quittent l&#39;usine, l&#39;équipe Qualité terrain est responsable de leur comportement en conditions réelles : des millions de trajets, en toutes saisons, dans des villes partout dans le monde. Vous travaillerez aux côtés d&#39;ingénieurs en qualité terrain pour aider à détecter les problèmes matériels émergents, à en investiguer la cause profonde et à soutenir la mise en place de correctifs avec les équipes d&#39;ingénierie, de fabrication et des opérations dans les marchés. Vous passerez du temps en laboratoire à manipuler des pièces défaillantes, et tout autant dans les données à évaluer l&#39;ampleur réelle d&#39;un problème.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsabilités :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Soutenir les analyses de défaillance sur des pièces retournées du terrain, y compris les demandes des clients entreprises, en participant au démontage, à l&#39;inspection et aux essais électriques et en documentant les constats avec photos.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Aider à surveiller les données terrain, comme les alertes des véhicules et des stations et les historiques de réparation, et signaler les problèmes émergents à l&#39;équipe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Concevoir et mettre à jour des tableaux de bord et des requêtes pour suivre les indicateurs de fiabilité et l&#39;avancement des mises à niveau.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participer aux campagnes de mise à niveau sur le terrain en aidant à repérer les unités touchées et en suivant l&#39;avancement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Aider à réviser les PON de réparation et les guides de diagnostic utilisés par les mécaniciens des marchés, et proposer des améliorations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribuer aux enquêtes sur les défaillances terrain dans Jira, en collaboration avec les ingénieurs, pour l&#39;analyse des causes profondes et les mesures correctives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Expérience :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Être inscrit ou inscrite à un programme de &lt;strong&gt;baccalauréat&lt;/strong&gt; ou de &lt;strong&gt;maîtrise&lt;/strong&gt; en génie mécanique, électrique, mécatronique ou industriel, ou dans un domaine connexe, dans une &lt;strong&gt;université canadienne, avec une fin d&#39;études prévue entre décembre 2027 et l&#39;été 2028 (obligatoire)&lt;/strong&gt;. Les personnes à la maîtrise ayant travaillé entre leurs deux programmes doivent cumuler moins de 2 ans d&#39;expérience à temps plein.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maîtrise professionnelle du &lt;strong&gt;français et de l&#39;anglais&lt;/strong&gt;, à l&#39;écrit comme à l&#39;oral (obligatoire)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Aisance à manipuler du matériel électromécanique, notamment le démontage, l&#39;inspection et le dépannage électrique de base avec des outils comme un multimètre&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solides compétences analytiques et aisance à travailler avec de grands ensembles de données imparfaits pour en tirer des conclusions claires&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connaissance des méthodes structurées de résolution de problèmes (5 pourquoi, diagramme d&#39;Ishikawa, 8D, AMDEC)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosité, souci du détail et communication écrite claire&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Un stage ou un stage coopératif antérieur en qualité, en fiabilité, en essais ou en analyse de défaillance constitue un atout&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;La connaissance de SQL ou de Python, ainsi qu&#39;une expérience avec Mode, Hex, Tableau ou Power BI, constituent un atout&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;La connaissance de Jira ou d&#39;outils de gestion de billets similaires constitue un atout&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une expérience avec les vélos électriques, les batteries, l&#39;automobile ou d&#39;autres produits électromécaniques, ou la lecture de schémas de câblage, constitue un atout&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Avantages :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Avantages en santé mentale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;En plus des jours fériés, les stagiaires bénéficient de 2 jours de congé payé et de 3 jours de congé de maladie&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Avantages de transport subventionnés et crédits de trajet Lyft&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Lyft s&#39;engage à créer un environnement de travail inclusif qui favorise l&#39;appartenance. Lyft estime que chaque personne a droit à l&#39;égalité des chances en matière d&#39;emploi, sans discrimination fondée sur la race, l&#39;ascendance, le lieu d&#39;origine, la couleur, l&#39;origine ethnique, la citoyenneté, les croyances, le sexe, l&#39;orientation sexuelle, l&#39;identité de genre, l&#39;expression de genre, l&#39;âge, l&#39;état matrimonial, la situation familiale, le handicap, l&#39;existence d&#39;un casier judiciaire gracié ou tout autre motif protégé par la loi applicable ou par la politique de l&#39;entreprise. Lyft s&#39;efforce également de créer un lieu de travail sain et sûr et interdit strictement tout harcèlement. Des aménagements pour les personnes handicapées seront fournis sur demande, conformément à la loi applicable, lors du processus de candidature et d&#39;embauche. Veuillez contacter votre recruteur si vous souhaitez faire une telle demande.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Ce poste s&#39;exerce à temps plein sur place, dans un établissement de Lyft. #Onsite&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;L&#39;échelle salariale de base prévue pour ce poste dans la région de Longueuil est de 34 $ à 36 $/heure CAD. Les échelles salariales varient en fonction de divers facteurs, notamment les qualifications, l&#39;expérience et la situation géographique. Votre recruteur pourra vous fournir davantage de précisions sur l&#39;échelle salariale propre à votre lieu de travail et sur les autres facteurs pris en compte durant le processus d&#39;embauche.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":4003537002,"name":"Early Talent","child_ids":[4081668002,4038876002,4037433002,4055195002,4037437002,4038882002,4038881002,4037603002],"parent_id":4042810002}],"offices":[{"id":4038242002,"name":"Montreal Office","location":"Montreal, Canada, Montreal","child_ids":[],"parent_id":4038337002}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":null,"ai_opt_out_request_url":null},{"absolute_url":"https://app.careerpuck.com/job-board/lyft/job/8817932002?gh_jid=8817932002","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"employment":"employment_optional","internal_job_id":6529045002,"location":{"name":"Longueuil, Canada"},"metadata":[{"id":4345907002,"name":"Career Site Category","value":"University","value_type":"single_select"}],"id":8817932002,"updated_at":"2026-10-19T18:43:36-04:00","requisition_id":"111199","title":"Stagiaire en ingénierie d'industrialisation (été 2027)","company_name":"Lyft","first_published":"2026-09-28T18:08:50-04:00","language":"fr","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;Chez Lyft, notre raison d&#39;être est de servir et de connecter. Lyft Urban Solutions conçoit, fabrique et exploite des systèmes de vélopartage dans plus de 50 villes à travers le monde, dont New York, Chicago, Londres, Barcelone, Mexico, Rio de Janeiro et Montréal. Notre usine de Longueuil est le berceau de BIXI, le premier système de vélopartage automatisé en Amérique du Nord, et fabrique aujourd&#39;hui les vélos et les stations de certains des plus grands réseaux de vélopartage au monde.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nous recherchons un ou une &lt;strong&gt;stagiaire en ingénierie d&#39;industrialisation&lt;/strong&gt; pour se joindre à notre équipe Ingénierie de la fabrication et de la qualité (Manufacturing &amp;amp; Quality Engineering) à notre usine de Longueuil. Vous travaillerez sur le plancher de production avec les équipes d&#39;assemblage, d&#39;entrepôt et de qualité afin de rendre nos procédés plus rapides, plus sécuritaires et plus constants. Vous ferez également partie d&#39;une équipe mondiale qui soutient des usines et des fournisseurs en Amérique du Nord et en Asie.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsabilités :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cartographier le flux de matières et l&#39;aménagement actuel de l&#39;usine et de l&#39;entrepôt, puis proposer des améliorations pour réduire le gaspillage et les déplacements des opérateurs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Réaliser des études de temps de cycle pour les opérations d&#39;assemblage et d&#39;entrepôt afin de repérer les goulots d&#39;étranglement et d&#39;améliorer le débit et l&#39;équilibrage des lignes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Auditer le respect des instructions d’assemblage sur le plancher, cerner les écarts et piloter les mesures correctives ou les mises à jour des instructions d’assemblage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diriger les audits 5S et mettre en place des contrôles visuels et des normes d&#39;organisation du milieu de travail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Concevoir des tableaux de bord pour suivre le débit, les encours, les temps de cycle et le respect des d’assemblage , et transformer les données en recommandations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Créer des instructions de travail visuelles, des fiches de travail standardisées.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribuer à des projets d&#39;amélioration continue, notamment des évaluations ergonomiques, la reconfiguration de postes de travail et l&#39;amélioration d&#39;outillages et de gabarits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Préparer les procédés en vue des modifications techniques (ECO) et des lancements de nouveaux produits, y compris les changements d&#39;aménagement et la validation des postes de travail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborer avec l&#39;équipe Qualité pour enquêter sur les défauts de production et contribuer à l&#39;analyse des causes profondes et à la mise à jour des risques par procédé (PFMEA).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Expérience :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Être inscrit ou inscrite à un programme de &lt;strong&gt;baccalauréat&lt;/strong&gt; ou de &lt;strong&gt;maîtrise&lt;/strong&gt; en génie industriel, en génie mécanique ou dans un domaine connexe dans une &lt;strong&gt;université canadienne, avec une fin d&#39;études prévue entre décembre 2027 et l&#39;été 2028 (obligatoire)&lt;/strong&gt;. Les personnes à la maîtrise ayant travaillé entre leurs deux programmes doivent cumuler moins de 2 ans d&#39;expérience à temps plein.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maîtrise professionnelle du &lt;strong&gt;français et de l&#39;anglais&lt;/strong&gt;, à l&#39;écrit comme à l&#39;oral (obligatoire)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connaissance pratique des principes de production allégée (juste-à-temps, travail standardisé, 5S, cartographie de la chaîne de valeur)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expérience avec AutoCAD ou un logiciel de CAO similaire pour la conception d&#39;aménagements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solides compétences analytiques et souci du détail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Aisance dans un environnement au rythme soutenu, avec la capacité de gérer plusieurs priorités selon l&#39;évolution des besoins sur le plancher&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Un stage ou un stage coopératif antérieur en fabrication, en opérations ou en qualité constitue un atout&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une expérience avec Mode, Hex, Tableau ou Power BI constitue un atout, tout comme la connaissance de SQL ou de Python&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;La connaissance de Jira ou d&#39;outils de gestion de billets similaires constitue un atout&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;La connaissance des systèmes PLM ou des processus de modification technique constitue un atou&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Avantages:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Avantages en santé mentale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;En plus des jours fériés, les stagiaires bénéficient de 2 jours de congé payé et de 3 jours de congé de maladie&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Avantages de transport subventionnés et crédits de trajet Lyft&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Lyft s&#39;engage à créer un environnement de travail inclusif qui favorise l&#39;appartenance. Lyft estime que chaque personne a droit à l&#39;égalité des chances en matière d&#39;emploi, sans discrimination fondée sur la race, l&#39;ascendance, le lieu d&#39;origine, la couleur, l&#39;origine ethnique, la citoyenneté, les croyances, le sexe, l&#39;orientation sexuelle, l&#39;identité de genre, l&#39;expression de genre, l&#39;âge, l&#39;état matrimonial, la situation familiale, le handicap, l&#39;existence d&#39;un casier judiciaire gracié ou tout autre motif protégé par la loi applicable ou par la politique de l&#39;entreprise. Lyft s&#39;efforce également de créer un lieu de travail sain et sûr et interdit strictement tout harcèlement. Des aménagements pour les personnes handicapées seront fournis sur demande, conformément à la loi applicable, lors du processus de candidature et d&#39;embauche. Veuillez contacter votre recruteur si vous souhaitez faire une telle demande.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Ce poste s&#39;exerce à temps plein sur place, dans un établissement de Lyft. #Onsite&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;L&#39;échelle salariale de base prévue pour ce poste dans la région de Longueuil est de 34 $ à 36 $/heure CAD. Les échelles salariales varient en fonction de divers facteurs, notamment les qualifications, l&#39;expérience et la situation géographique. Votre recruteur pourra vous fournir davantage de précisions sur l&#39;échelle salariale propre à votre lieu de travail et sur les autres facteurs pris en compte durant le processus d&#39;embauche.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":4003537002,"name":"Early Talent","child_ids":[4081668002,4038876002,4037433002,4055195002,4037437002,4038882002,4038881002,4037603002],"parent_id":4042810002}],"offices":[{"id":4049383002,"name":"Longueuil Office","location":"Longueuil, Quebec, Canada","child_ids":[],"parent_id":4038337002}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":null,"ai_opt_out_request_url":null},{"absolute_url":"https://app.careerpuck.com/job-board/lyft/job/8814971002?gh_jid=8814971002","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"education":"education_optional","employment":"employment_required","internal_job_id":6527856002,"location":{"name":"Toronto, Canada"},"metadata":[{"id":4345907002,"name":"Career Site Category","value":"Accounting & Finance","value_type":"single_select"}],"id":8814971002,"updated_at":"2026-10-19T18:43:36-04:00","requisition_id":"111194","title":"Treasury Analyst","company_name":"Lyft","first_published":"2026-09-23T14:38:01-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;At Lyft, our purpose is to serve and connect. We aim to achieve this by cultivating a work environment where all team members belong and have the opportunity to thrive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re hiring a Treasury Analyst to join our Treasury team at a pivotal moment — we&#39;re actively integrating recent acquisitions, implementing a new Treasury Management System, and scaling our banking infrastructure across a rapidly growing international footprint supporting Lyft’s core, autonomous, and luxury offerings. This is a hands-on role with real ownership from day one.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Head of Treasury, you&#39;ll support critical functional areas and workstreams including cash management, liquidity optimization, and SOX compliance, while getting exposure to strategic projects that shape how Treasury operates across the company. If you&#39;re intellectually curious, detail-oriented, and energized by a fast-moving environment, you&#39;ll thrive here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Treasury Operations&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Position cash daily for Lyft&#39;s parent and subsidiary entities across North America, optimizing liquidity at the bank account and legal entity level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support Lyft&#39;s global banking infrastructure: the master account repository, authorized signatory records, registration/regulatory documentation, and banking product subscriptions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute and monitor electronic payment requests, trade settlements, and other cash movements critical to the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support letters of credit — issuance, renewal, and cancellation - and maintain accurate records and track related expenses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the Treasury Management System (TMS) implementation and the subsequent process migration, including process design, parallel testing, and SOP documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a liaison to internal and external partners, responding to inquiries and resolving ad hoc issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help identify and build AI-assisted automation for repetitive Treasury tasks, driving operational efficiency across the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure adherence to Treasury policies, protocols, and internal controls to maintain compliance and mitigate risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support internal SOX and external audit requests related to Treasury processes and controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support M&amp;amp;A due diligence and post M&amp;amp;A integration workstreams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in other ad hoc projects as Treasury&#39;s priorities evolve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BS/BA in Finance, Economics, Business, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of 2 years of professional experience in Corporate Treasury or a related financial function.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with online banking platforms, payment methods, and common corporate banking products and services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Google Suite (Gmail, Sheets, Docs, Slides).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in English with strong verbal and written communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong work ethic, high accountability, and a collaborative mindset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort operating in a fast-paced environment with frequently shifting priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional attention to detail, organization, and time management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred:&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working for a multinational, publicly traded company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using a Treasury Management System (e.g. Kyriba, FIS, GTreasury).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing and building financial models from scratch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using AI assistants (e.g., Claude, ChatGPT, Gemini) to improve results and process efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with payment service providers, merchant processors, or gateways.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Project management experience and skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexibility to occasionally work early mornings or evenings to support European time zones and critical deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extended health and dental coverage options, along with life insurance and disability benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family building benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Child care and pet benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to a Lyft funded Health Care Savings Account&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;RRSP plan with company match to help save for your future&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In addition to provincial observed holidays, salaried team members are covered under Lyft&#39;s flexible paid time off policy. The policy allows team members to take off as much time as they need (with manager approval). Hourly team members get 15 days paid time off, with an additional day for each year of service&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lyft is proud to support new parents with 18 weeks of paid time off, designed as a top-up plan to complement provincial programs. Biological, adoptive, and foster parents are all eligible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subsidized commuter benefits and Lyft ride credits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lyft is committed to creating an inclusive workforce that fosters belonging. Lyft believes that every person has a right to equal employment opportunities without discrimination because of race, ancestry, place of origin, colour, ethnic origin, citizenship, creed, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, marital status, family status, disability, pardoned record of offences, or any other basis protected by applicable law or by Company policy. Lyft also strives for a healthy and safe workplace and strictly prohibits harassment of any kind.&amp;nbsp; Accommodation for persons with disabilities will be provided upon request in accordance with applicable law during the application and hiring process. Please contact your recruiter if you wish to make such a request.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lyft highly values having employees working in-office to foster a collaborative work environment and company culture. This role will be in-office on a hybrid schedule — Team Members will be expected to work in the office at least 3 days per week, including on Mondays, Wednesdays, and Thursdays. Lyft considers working in the office at least 3 days per week to be an essential function of this hybrid role. Your recruiter can share more information about the various in-office perks Lyft offers. Additionally, hybrid roles have the flexibility to work from anywhere for up to 4 weeks per year. #Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The expected base pay range for this position in the Toronto area is CAD $84,000 - CAD $105,000, not inclusive of potential equity offering, bonus or benefits. Salary ranges are dependent on a variety of factors, including qualifications, experience and geographic location. Your recruiter can share more information about the salary range specific to your working location and other factors during the hiring process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lyft may use artificial intelligence to screen applicants, however, Lyft employees make the ultimate selection and hiring decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This job fills an existing vacancy.&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":4082056002,"name":"Treasury","child_ids":[],"parent_id":4002291002}],"offices":[{"id":4080790002,"name":"Toronto Coworking","location":"Toronto, Ontario, Canada","child_ids":[],"parent_id":4038336002}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":null,"ai_opt_out_request_url":null},{"absolute_url":"https://app.careerpuck.com/job-board/lyft/job/8896666002?gh_jid=8896666002","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"education":"education_required","employment":"employment_required","internal_job_id":6563460002,"location":{"name":"New York, NY"},"metadata":[{"id":4345907002,"name":"Career Site Category","value":"User Experience Research","value_type":"single_select"}],"id":8896666002,"updated_at":"2026-10-20T16:46:07-04:00","requisition_id":"111266","title":"UX Researcher","company_name":"Lyft","first_published":"2026-10-16T22:16:57-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Job ID: 111266&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Lyft, our purpose is to serve and connect. We aim to achieve this by cultivating a work environment where all team members belong and have the opportunity to thrive.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and conduct studies across key product areas, utilizing methods such as&amp;nbsp;ethnographic/field research, surveys, concept testing, usability testing, and any other&amp;nbsp;methods you find impactful.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with our data scientists to provide qualitative context for their quantitative insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review, analyze, and communicate mixed methods data to generate tactical and strategic insights, as well as actionable recommendations that drive product innovation and design improvements for users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Find creative and compelling ways to generate, present, and evangelize results and recommendations throughout the company, in order to help cultivate a highly informed, more effective, and more empathetic organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with cross-functional partners to shape product direction based on research findings and follow-up with partners about implementation to understand how findings are being used.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Education and Experience:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master&#39;s degree or foreign equivalent in psychology, data analysis, statistics, or&amp;nbsp;related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1 year of experience in job offered, data analysis, or related occupation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Skills:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with research and statistical analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience conducting qualitative and quantitative research.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience analyzing data surveys, experimental studies, content analysis, and correlational research.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Great medical, dental, and vision insurance options with additional programs available when enrolled&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family building benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Child care and pet benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) plan to help save for your future&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In addition to 12 observed holidays, salaried team members have discretionary paid time off, hourly team members have 15 days paid time off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;18 weeks of paid parental leave. Biological, adoptive, and foster parents are all eligible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subsidized commuter benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lyft Pink - Lyft team members get an exclusive opportunity to test new benefits of our Ridership Program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Lyft is an equal opportunity employer committed to an inclusive workplace that fosters belonging. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regards to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, age, genetic information, or any other basis prohibited by law. We also consider qualified applicants with criminal histories consistent with applicable federal, state and local law.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Lyft highly values having employees working in-office to foster a collaborative work environment and company culture. This role will be in-office on a hybrid schedule — Team Members will be expected to work in the office 3 days per week on Mondays, Wednesdays, and Thursdays. Lyft considers working in the office at least 3 days per week to be an essential function of this hybrid role. Your recruiter can share more information about the various in-office perks Lyft offers. Additionally, hybrid roles have the flexibility to work from anywhere for up to 4 weeks per year. #Hybrid&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;The expected base pay range for this position in the New York City area is $128,000 - $192,000/year. Salary ranges are dependent on a variety of factors, including qualifications, experience and geographic location. Range is not inclusive of potential equity offering, bonus or benefits. Your recruiter can share more information about the salary range specific to your working location and other factors during the hiring process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;#LI-DNI&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":4140217002,"name":"Design & UX Research","child_ids":[],"parent_id":4140216002}],"offices":[{"id":4000997002,"name":"New York Office","location":"New York, New York, United States","child_ids":[],"parent_id":4032338002}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":null,"ai_opt_out_request_url":null},{"absolute_url":"https://app.careerpuck.com/job-board/lyft/job/8797069002?gh_jid=8797069002","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"employment":"employment_optional","internal_job_id":6519728002,"location":{"name":"Toronto, Canada"},"metadata":[{"id":4345907002,"name":"Career Site Category","value":"University","value_type":"single_select"}],"id":8797069002,"updated_at":"2026-10-19T18:43:36-04:00","requisition_id":"111172","title":"UX Research Intern (Summer 2027)","company_name":"Lyft","first_published":"2026-09-11T13:50:25-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;At Lyft, our purpose is to serve and connect. We aim to achieve this by cultivating a work environment where all team members belong and have the opportunity to thrive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lyft is seeking a Mixed Methods User Experience Research Intern to join our team, which aspires to elevate the user experience for our drivers and riders across 300+ cities nationwide. You will conduct research studies, as well as participate in studies alongside more senior researchers from which you’ll gain strong mentorship. You will partner with Design, Product Management, Analytics, and Engineering in order to derive deep insights about our users’ behaviors and attitudes, and communicate results and actionable recommendations across the company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Interns contribute to user-facing products, working side-by-side with top User Experience Research team members in the industry while having autonomy from the get-go. Lyft fosters a collaborative environment in the office, so there&#39;s always a sharp mind eager to hear about your next idea. So what&#39;s yours?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and conduct studies across key Lyft product areas -- independently and in conjunction with more senior researchers. You will utilize methods such as ethnographic &amp;amp; field research, diary studies, surveys, user/usability testing (remote and in-person), guerrilla research, and any other methods you find impactful&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review, analyze, and communicate qualitative and/or quantitative data to generate tactical and strategic insights, as well as actionable recommendations which drive product innovation and design improvements for users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Currently pursuing a&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Bachelor&#39;s, &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Master&#39;s&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;or &lt;strong&gt;PhD degree &lt;/strong&gt;in Human-Computer Interaction, Anthropology, Design, Psychology, Cognitive Science, or a related field from a &lt;strong&gt;university in&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Canada&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt; with a&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;graduation date between December 2027 and Summer 2028 (required)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Available during &lt;strong&gt;Summer 2027&lt;/strong&gt; for an internship in&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Toronto&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extraordinary organizational skills and meticulous eye for detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong listening and analytical skills; proactive troubleshooter&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team player with excellent written &amp;amp; verbal communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enthusiasm for a collaborative, highly energetic, fun and fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience as a researcher and/or research coordinator for qualitative research studies or school-based research projects, including usability/user testing, surveys, field research, or user interviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research experience with mobile technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience conducting qualitative research in applied research settings, ideally within a Product organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing surveys and experimental research, and analyzing large datasets using appropriate statistical methods&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using Qualtrics or SurveyMonkey&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience cleaning, handling, and transforming data in Microsoft Excel and/or Google Sheets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with SQL, R, and/or other data analysis software (e.g., SPSS)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with research participant recruitment and management practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design thinking, visual communication, information design, or wireframing skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In addition to holidays, interns receive 2 days paid time off and 3 days sick time off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subsidized commuter benefits and Lyft ride credits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Lyft is committed to creating an inclusive workforce that fosters belonging. Lyft believes that every person has a right to equal employment opportunities without discrimination because of race, ancestry, place of origin, colour, ethnic origin, citizenship, creed, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, marital status, family status, disability, pardoned record of offences, or any other basis protected by applicable law or by Company policy. Lyft also strives for a healthy and safe workplace and strictly prohibits harassment of any kind.&amp;nbsp; Accommodation for persons with disabilities will be provided upon request in accordance with applicable law during the application and hiring process. Please contact your recruiter if you wish to make such a request.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Lyft highly values having employees working in-office to foster a collaborative work environment and company culture. This role will be in-office on a hybrid schedule — Team Members will be expected to work in the office at least 3 days per week, including on Mondays, Wednesdays, and Thursdays. Lyft considers working in the office at least 3 days per week to be an essential function of this hybrid role. Your recruiter can share more information about the various in-office perks Lyft offers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The expected base pay range for this position in the Toronto area is CAD $40 - CAD $48 per hour. Salary ranges are dependent on a variety of factors, including qualifications, experience and geographic location. Your recruiter can share more information about the salary range specific to your working location and other factors during the hiring process.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s1&quot;&gt;Lyft may use artificial intelligence to screen applicants, however, Lyft employees make the ultimate selection and hiring decisions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s1&quot;&gt;This is a new position.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":4003537002,"name":"Early Talent","child_ids":[4081668002,4038876002,4037433002,4055195002,4037437002,4038882002,4038881002,4037603002],"parent_id":4042810002}],"offices":[{"id":4139788002,"name":"Toronto Office","location":"Toronto, Canada, Toronto","child_ids":[],"parent_id":4038198002}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":null,"ai_opt_out_request_url":null},{"absolute_url":"https://app.careerpuck.com/job-board/lyft/job/8834157002?gh_jid=8834157002","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"education":"education_optional","employment":"employment_required","internal_job_id":6536553002,"location":{"name":"San Francisco, CA"},"metadata":[{"id":4345907002,"name":"Career Site Category","value":"People","value_type":"single_select"}],"id":8834157002,"updated_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:33-04:00","requisition_id":"111209","title":"VP, People","company_name":"Lyft","first_published":"2026-09-23T12:29:07-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;At Lyft, our purpose is to serve and connect. We aim to achieve this by cultivating a work environment where all team members belong and have the opportunity to thrive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lyft is in a defining moment: accelerating growth, expanding internationally, and building the world&#39;s leading hybrid rideshare network. How we build, organize, and lead our people will determine how well we get there. As Vice President, People, you will help drive the business forward through the strength of our people strategy, serving as a right hand to our Chief People Officer and a trusted advisor to Lyft&#39;s executive leadership team. This is a high-impact role for a seasoned people executive who operates at altitude and on the ground in equal measure, thrives in fast-paced, dynamic environments, and is energized by the chance to own some of the most complex and consequential work in the function.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Chief People Officer, you will lead the People Business Partner organization, own workforce planning for the enterprise, and drive the human capital strategy behind Lyft&#39;s M&amp;amp;A activity from diligence through integration. You&#39;ll partner directly with the executive leadership team, represent the People function in cross-functional forums, and shape the org design, structure and ways of working that will carry Lyft into its next chapter. You&#39;ll anticipate challenges, help leaders look around corners, and bring forward-thinking solutions to keep Lyft&#39;s workforce agile, engaged, and ready for the future while shaping how the People function itself grows from here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join us and help shape the future of work at one of the most mission-driven, people-focused companies redefining mobility.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Executive Partnership &amp;amp; People Strategy&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner directly with the Chief People Officer and executive leadership team on the people strategy behind Lyft&#39;s most significant business decisions, acting as a trusted advisor and bringing best-in-class practices to enable growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;People Business Partnering &amp;amp; Org Leadership&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the Global People Business Partner function (team of 14) end to end across Lyft&#39;s global footprint — strategy, structure, and team leadership — driving organizational effectiveness and modernizing how the function delivers value at scale across every market, region, and legal entity we operate in. Get into the details when it matters — from a thorny org design problem to a retention conversation with a critical hire.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anticipate workforce challenges and guide leaders through complex organizational change with empathy and strategic foresight&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape scalable team structures and influence how Lyft builds leadership pipelines, attracts, develops, and retains top talent across the company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, empower, and develop a team of high-performing People Business Partners, fostering a culture of strategic impact, continuous growth, and bench strength for the function&#39;s next generation of leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;M&amp;amp;A Human Capital&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the human capital workstream for Lyft&#39;s international M&amp;amp;A activity, including cultural and talent due diligence, retention-risk assessment, org design and integration planning, comp and benefits harmonization, and Day 1 readiness for newly acquired teams — including cross-border and works-council considerations. You&#39;re as comfortable running the details of a deal integration as you are advising the executive team on strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Workforce Planning &amp;amp; Future of Work&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own enterprise workforce planning in partnership with Finance — multi-year headcount and skills planning, scenario and contingency planning, and workforce analytics that inform where and how Lyft invests in talent globally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Team Member Experience and Tech to help our people and teams grow alongside new tools and technology; from emerging skills needs to how we work together most effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Cross-Functional Partnership&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with other Centers of Excellence (Talent Acquisition, Team Member Experience, Total Rewards, People Operations, Culture &amp;amp; Belonging) and with Legal to enable programs that create meaningful business impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with People Systems &amp;amp; Operations to modernize team member self-service capabilities through technology and automation, and drive adoption across the business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years of progressive HR leadership experience, including prior experience operating at the VP or Head of People level, partnering with C-suite and board-level stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ownership of HR-side M&amp;amp;A diligence and integration — ideally including cross-border or multi-entity integration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ownership of strategic, skills-based workforce planning at an enterprise level, in close partnership with Finance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in the tech industry, at public companies, and in growth or marketplace organizations will all be considered favorably, but are not necessarily required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to influence and coach senior executives and drive strategic people decisions at the enterprise level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven success leading and coaching a team of high-performing people business partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong business acumen with the ability to understand industry dynamics and align people strategies with business priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to thrive in ambiguity and lead through change in a dynamic environment, modernizing the People function and building a best-in-class team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data- and insights-driven mindset to measure success and continuously improve people strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep commitment to inclusion, belonging, and culture-building as a competitive advantage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills, with the ability to engage a variety of audiences — including the executive team — on complex people topics, and to challenge the status quo as appropriate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to establish relationships and credibility at all levels of the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highest level of integrity and commitment to managing confidential information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Great medical, dental, and vision insurance options with additional programs available when enrolled&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family building benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Child care and pet benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) plan to help save for your future&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In addition to 12 observed holidays, salaried team members have discretionary paid time off, hourly team members have 15 days paid time off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;18 weeks of paid parental leave. Biological, adoptive, and foster parents are all eligible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subsidized commuter benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lyft Pink - Lyft team members get an exclusive opportunity to test new benefits of our Ridership Program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Lyft is an equal opportunity employer committed to an inclusive workplace that fosters belonging. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regards to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, age, genetic information, or any other basis prohibited by law. We also consider qualified applicants with criminal histories consistent with applicable federal, state and local law.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Lyft highly values having employees working in-office to foster a collaborative work environment and company culture. This role will be in-office on a hybrid schedule — Team Members will be expected to work in the office 3 days per week on Mondays, Wednesdays, and Thursdays. Lyft considers working in the office at least 3 days per week to be an essential function of this hybrid role. Your recruiter can share more information about the various in-office perks Lyft offers. Additionally, hybrid roles have the flexibility to work from anywhere for up to 4 weeks per year. #Hybrid&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The expected base pay range for this position in San Francisco is $300-$325K. In addition to the base pay, this role is eligible for competitive equity awards, bonuses, and benefits. You can read more about Lyft’s employee benefits &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.lyft.com/careers/life-at-lyft&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Total compensation is dependent on a variety of factors, including qualifications, experience, and geographic location. Your recruiter can share more information about the salary range specific to your working location and other factors during the hiring process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":4038190002,"name":"Executive","child_ids":[4047184002,4048791002,4053407002,4047188002,4112306002,4047190002,4053405002,4055377002,4047189002,4047185002,4065652002,4081661002,4047187002,4047191002,4053408002,4056422002,4051163002,4053406002,4047186002],"parent_id":null}],"offices":[{"id":4000998002,"name":"San Francisco Office","location":"San Francisco, California, United States","child_ids":[],"parent_id":4031979002}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":null,"ai_opt_out_request_url":null}],"meta":{"total":179}}
